{"parentUuid":"cc7f7656-e975-4915-84e8-ced6739adbfb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016CukGAoT8bWUJ8pvzB1h1R","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Executed 7 commands (694 lines, 48.0KB). Indexed 20 sections. Searched 7 queries.\n\n## Commands\n\n- SB meetings Aug-Sep listing: `ls -la ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings/ | grep -E '2026-0(8-(1|2|3)|9)' ; ls ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/status-log/ ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/status-reports/ 2>&1 | tail -40; ls ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/*interview* 2>&1; ls ~/SecondBrain/Projects/ ~/SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026/ 2>&1`\n- SB grep keyword files: `cd ~/SecondBrain && for k in 'NCAA' 'attestation' 'continuity' 'Tech Inventory|tech inventory|Tech_Inventory' 'Toby' 'curriculum|Curriculum' 'Return to Performance|return to performance|RTP' 'protocol manual|Create the Manual|HPI protocol' 'Staged to Fall|staged to fall' 'Fall OKR|fall OKR'; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -rlE \"$k\" --include='*.md' . 2>/dev/null | xargs ls -t 2>/dev/null | head -15; done`\n- portfolio json matching entries: `cd ~/DEV/project-triage && python3 -c \" import json,re d=json.load(open('portfolio.json')) print(type(d), list(d.keys()) if isinstance(d,dict) else len(d)) s=json.dumps(d) for k in d if isinstance(d,dict) else []: v=d[k] if isinstance(v,list): for e in v: t=json.dumps(e) if re.search(r'Tech_Inventory|SoftwareTech|Curriculum|RTP|Return|HPI|Manual|NCAA|Staged|Fall',t,re.I): print('---',k); print(json.dumps(e,indent=1)[:2500]) \"`\n- memory files rtp tech ath: `cd ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/ && cat project_rtp-cla-course.md project_tech-inventory-refresh.md project_ath-tech-framework.md project_status-report-sourcing.md`\n- DEV area index greps: `cd ~/DEV && grep -nEi 'inventory|curricul|rtp|return.to|hpi|manual|ncaa|toby|cla' PERFORMANCE.md PROGRAM.md RESEARCH.md PLATFORM.md FOOTBALL.md 2>/dev/null`\n- memsearch queries: `for q in 'NCAA webinar data technology best practices continuity plan' 'NCAA attestation report' 'Toby Brooks curriculum' 'Return to Performance course Joe session builder' 'HPI protocol manual Kenny'; do echo \"=== $q\"; memsearch search \"$q\" --top-k 5 2>&1 | head -60; done`\n- Drive find NCAA and related: `cd \"$HOME/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive\" && find . -maxdepth 5 \\( -iname '*ncaa*' -o -iname '*attestation*' -o -iname '*continuity*' -o -iname '*inventory*' -o -iname '*curricul*' -o -iname '*manual*' -o -iname '*return*perform*' \\) -not -path '*DexaProject*' 2>/dev/null | head -60`\n\n## Indexed Sections\n\n- SB meetings Aug-Sep listing (1) (4.0KB)\n- SB meetings Aug-Sep listing (2) (0.3KB)\n- SB grep keyword files (1) (0.4KB)\n- SB grep keyword files (2) (5.8KB)\n- portfolio json matching entries (1) (0.5KB)\n- portfolio json matching entries (2) (12.0KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (0.2KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (0.3KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (1.1KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (0.3KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (3.7KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (0.3KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (1.9KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (0.3KB)\n- memory files rtp tech ath (1.7KB)\n- DEV area index greps (1) (0.2KB)\n- DEV area index greps (2) (8.7KB)\n- memsearch queries (0.4KB)\n- Drive find NCAA and related (1) (0.4KB)\n- Drive find NCAA and related (2) (5.7KB)\n\n## NCAA webinar data technology recommendations\n\n### Drive find NCAA and related (2)\n…lum\n./07_EDUCATION/Baylor_Applied Performance_Intern Curriculum/FA2026_ClemsonInternCurriculum_Sample.zip\n./02_SPORTS/Cheer/SUM2026/BU_Cheer_Summer_Training_Manual_2026_v2.docx\n./02_SPORTS/Cheer/SUM2026/BU_Cheer_Summer_Training_Manual_2026.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/ValdPerformance/ForceDecks/VALD Normative Data Report – 2024-25 NFL and NCAA Football Report.pdf\n./05_SYSTEMS/DEV_Backup/BU-1979FJ4/CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum\n./05_SYSTEMS/DEV_Backup/BU-1979FJ4/Education_Alignment_Initiative/2025-12-16_Performance_Education_Curriculum_Map.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/DEV_Backup/BU-1979FJ4/AppliedUtilization/Technology_Team_Inventory.md\n./05_SYSTEMS/ActionApps/SUM2025_PerformanceNFLNCAAFB_Demo_PBIreport.pdf\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-09-01_.pdf\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-09-01_.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/TechInventory_…\n\n…ory_2026-08/Tech_Inventory_FINDINGS_ER_2026-08-29.pdf\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/TechInventory_2026-08/Tech_Inventory_FINDINGS_ER_2026-08-29.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/TechInventory_2026-08/Tech_Inventory_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-09-01.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/TechInventory_2026-08/data/tech_inventory_long.csv\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_TECH_LISTS_ER_2026-09-01_.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/NCAA_PerformanceTech_v3.docx\n./05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_TECH_LISTS_ER_2026-09-01_.pdf\n./10_ARCHIVE/Health_and_Wellness/GENERAL/HW PP Inventory.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2025-12-03_Education_Alignment_Initative/2025-12-16_Performance_Education_Curriculum_Map.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026_Scouting_Academy/Scouting-Academy-Curriculum-Critical-Factors.pdf\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-05-06_Strategic_Plan_2026/NCAA_SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations_V1.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_Performance_Tech_Action_Plan.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_Performance_Tech_Action_Plan_DETAILED.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_PerformanceTech_Condensed.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_PerformanceTech_Condensed_v2.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/Copies/NCAA_SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations - Copy.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/Copies/NCAA_Performance_Tech_Action_Plan - Copy.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/Copies/NCAA_PerformanceTech_Condensed - Copy.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/Copies/NCAA_SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations_V1.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_PerformanceTech_v3.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/NCAA_SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations_V1.docx\n./01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/graphify-out/converted/HPI_RTP_Manual_Outline_V3_b525cf0\n\n### memory files rtp tech ath\nBaylor Athletics software & technology management framework. Lives at\n`~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/deliverables/`.\n\n**Shipped set — 2026-08-14** (four documents, `.docx` + `.pdf` of each):\n- `Software_and_Tech_Management_ER_2026-08-14` — the framework itself, including\n  Appendix A, the NCAA performance-technology crosswalk (`NCAA_PerformanceTech_v3.docx`).\n- `Software_and_Tech_Management_WORKFLOW_ER_2026-08-14` — the request/approval workflow.\n- `Software_and_Tech_Management_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-08-14` — the exec summary.\n- Intake forms: `Form_1_Technology_Idea_Form.docx` (requester),\n  `Form_2_Internal_ATH_Form.docx` (internal), `Request_Tracker.xlsx`.\n\nEarlier drafts in the same folder carry `DRAFT`, `SUPERSEDED_pre-edit`, or an older date\nin the filename. **The `2026-08-14` stamp is the live set** — there is no `_Archive/`\nsubfolder here, so read the date, not the folder.\n\n**Still missing from the framework** (known gaps as of 2026-08-14, none written yet):\nEducation section · Working Group definition · transfer student-athlete handling ·\nconsent template · annual survey.\n\n**Blocked on:** the ITS intake path. Micah is the contact who can supply it; the\nframework cannot state how a request actually reaches ITS until that meeting happens.\nThe separate inventory email to staff is the other open action.\n\n**Why:** the shipped/draft distinction is invisible from the filenames alone, and the\nfive gaps are not marked inside the documents — they only ever lived in working memory.\n\n**How to apply:** when asked to revise or extend the framework, start from the\n`2026-08-14` files, never a `DRAFT` or `_` variant. Do not treat the five gaps as\noversights to fix silently — Education and Working Group in particular need Micah's\nITS answer first. Related: [[status-report-sourcing]] (this is a recurring \"Shipped\"\nline item), [[kenny-boyd-doc-review-preferences]] (tone rules for the review pass).\n\n### memsearch queries\n# memsearch queries\n\n$ for q in 'NCAA webinar data technology best practices continuity plan' 'NCAA attestation report' 'Toby Brooks curriculum' 'Return to Performance course Joe session builder' 'HPI protocol manual Kenny'; do echo \"=== $q\"; memsearch search \"$q\" --top-k 5 2>&1 | head -60; done\n\n/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/.ctx-mode-yXyFzs/script.sh:2: parse error near `for'\n\n## NCAA attestation report\n\n### memsearch queries\n# memsearch queries\n\n$ for q in 'NCAA webinar data technology best practices continuity plan' 'NCAA attestation report' 'Toby Brooks curriculum' 'Return to Performance course Joe session builder' 'HPI protocol manual Kenny'; do echo \"=== $q\"; memsearch search \"$q\" --top-k 5 2>&1 | head -60; done\n\n/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/.ctx-mode-yXyFzs/script.sh:2: parse error near `for'\n\n### Drive find NCAA and related (1)\n# Drive find NCAA and related\n\n$ cd \"$HOME/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive\" && find . -maxdepth 5 \\( -iname '*ncaa*' -o -iname '*attestation*' -o -iname '*continuity*' -o -iname '*inventory*' -o -iname '*curricul*' -o -iname '*manual*' -o -iname '*return*perform*' \\) -not -path '*DexaProject*' 2>/dev/null | head -60\n\n### SB grep keyword files (1)\n# SB grep keyword files\n\n$ cd ~/SecondBrain && for k in 'NCAA' 'attestation' 'continuity' 'Tech Inventory|tech inventory|Tech_Inventory' 'Toby' 'curriculum|Curriculum' 'Return to Performance|return to performance|RTP' 'protocol manual|Create the Manual|HPI protocol' 'Staged to Fall|staged to fall' 'Fall OKR|fall OKR'; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -rlE \"$k\" --include='*.md' . 2>/dev/null | xargs ls -t 2>/dev/null | head -15; done\n\n## Tech inventory deadline 9/29 Kenny\n\n### memory files rtp tech ath\nAnalysis project: `~/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis` (**not a git repo** — nothing to\ncommit there). Survey data feeds the framework in `~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework`.\n\n**The forms-platform trap.** The live survey runs on **Microsoft Forms**. The 08-29\nexport header row proves it: `ID · Start time · Completion time · Email · Name ·\nLast modified time`. But `SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/docs/INVENTORY_FORMS_LINKS.md`\ndocuments two **Google** Forms with real form IDs. The Google forms are 08-13\nproposal-era prototypes — their dropdown has 26 options against the 33 units in\n`clean/coverage.csv`.\n\n**Consequence:** `gws` can reach those Google form IDs and will return few or no\nresponses. T…\n\n…negative**, not evidence that nobody new replied.\nLive responses cannot be reached from the CLI at all. Eric must download the\nexport from Microsoft Forms by hand.\n\n**Baseline checked 2026-09-07** (verified against the .xlsx itself, not the derived\nCSV): newest export anywhere on disk is `raw/Quick_Inventory_export_2026-08-29.xlsx`\n— 37 responses, 27 of 33 units, 147 distinct technologies. The OneDrive copy at\n`~/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/Documents/` is byte-identical\n(same md5). Nothing newer exists in `~`.\n\n**Two OneDrive copies — one is stale.** `OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/Documents/\nQuick_Inventory_export_2026-08-29.xlsx` is current. But\n`OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/Athletics Technology - Quick Inventory.xlsx`, at the\nOneDrive **root** with the survey's display name, is the **08-24** export — md5\n`0f7874bbddb3cc10592805687aff6ea1`, identical to `raw/..._2026-08-24.xlsx`. Eric\nlinked that root file on 2026-09-08 believing it was the update. Its friendly name\nmakes it look canonical; it is f…\n\n…days behind. Always md5 an OneDrive copy against\n`raw/` before treating it as new.\n\nUnits with no response: Golf (M) · Tennis (M) · Tennis (W) · Volleyball ·\nBusiness Office. `Other` also shows zero but is a catch-all box, not a department —\ndo not report it as a sixth missing unit. Department soft deadline: **29 September 2026**,\nso gaps before then are expected, not a coverage failure.\n\n**Reminder sent 2026-09-08.** Eric emailed all five non-responding units as five\nseparate per-unit notes (not one group email), with a **Tuesday 29 September**\ndeadline. He edited the wording himself before sending, so the file record is the\nask, not a transcript: `~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/docs/\nINVENTORY_REMINDER_2026-09-08-sent.md`. **Kenny Boyd and Jovon Overshown were\ndeliberately left off the CC** — the 08-13 original CC'd them, and holding that\nback keeps it available as escalation for a second reminder. Do not suggest\nsending a first reminder again; the open question is now whether responses arrived.\n\n**Refresh path:** save the download as `raw/Quick_Inventory_export_YYYY-MM-DD.xlsx`\n(never edit `raw/`), then\n`cd ~/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis && uv run --with openpyxl python3 scripts/clean_inventory.py`.\nThe script always picks the newest `raw/` file. Then co…\n\n### portfolio json matching entries (2)\n<class 'dict'> ['meta', 'projects', 'ideas', 'inbox']\n--- projects\n{\n \"name\": \"Tech_Inventory_Analysis\",\n \"lane\": \"job\",\n \"rank\": 16,\n \"status\": \"active\",\n \"stage\": \"building\",\n \"purpose\": \"Clean and analyze the Baylor Athletics Technology Inventory survey (Microsoft Forms Quick Inventory, 5 questions). Turns free-text departmental answers into a tidy one-row-per-technology inventory, a coverage map against the 26 sport/unit list, and a screening list of athlete-data systems that feeds the Detailed 17-question second pass. Data collection companion to SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework, which holds the framework, form specs and form links.\",\n \"next_action\": \"Follow up with the five outstanding units before the 29 September department soft deadline - Golf (M), Tennis (M), Tennis (W), Volleyball, Business Office. Then re-export, re-run the pipeline, and every document rebuilds with final numbers. Still unidentified: SCRL app and JABA.\",\n \"dev_folder\": \"Tech_Inventory_Analysis\",\n \"links\": [\n  \"https://claude.ai/code/artifact/42a7b360-2add-41f3-9d5f-2cc5f17141c8\"\n ],\n \"updates\": [\n  {\n   \"date\": \"2026-08-30\",\n   \"note\": \"Added a Word version (scripts/build_docx.py -> Tech_Inventory_FINDINGS_ER_2026-08-29.docx, 8 data tables built from the CSVs so it cannot drift, Baylor-green headings, branding in the header and document status on every page per Kenny's review history). Reviewed the meeting transcripts for what deliverable Kenny actually wants and found two things. First, a correction: 29 August was Applied Performance's own deadline, but the 2026-08-24 all-staff meeting set a department-wide SOFT DEADLINE of 29 SEPTEMBER with unit leaders assigning staff - so collection is still open and the five non-responding units are outstanding, not delinquent. The report, PDF, HTML and markdown were all reframed as an interim read, and blame-adjacent phrasing ('nothing in the current process notices this', 'open exposure with no owner') was rewritten as forward-looking capability language. Second, the deliverable: at the 2026-08-13 review Kenny asked for 'the more simple and concise, almost like one page checklist' and closed with 'I do think we need to figure out all the systems that we're using', which Jon Allen framed as 'nobody knows everything that exists' at 80-90% known. The inventory IS Kenny's ask, but a 10-page report is