eamlit app → own `CLAUDE.md`; disk is the source of truth, the Claude cloud project `StaffProject_BE` is only a pointer. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:15:| `ValdReport/` | VALD reporting. Has `index.html` micro-app → own `CLAUDE.md` |\nPERFORMANCE.md:16:| `VALD_Performance/` | ForceDecks monitoring pipeline (PowerShell, Python, MATLAB) that builds and refreshes the `VALD_Monitoring_Football` workbook from raw VALD Hub exports. Own `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md`. Git repo, created 2026-09-14 on Windows. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:17:| `VALD_Release/` | VALD records release work: release documents, the email knowledge base, and what was sent to whom. Own `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md`. Git repo, created 2026-09-14 on Windows. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:24:| `Risk_Stratification_Engine/` | Risk stratification → own `CLAUDE.md` |\nPERFORMANCE.md:26:| `Injury_Surveillance/` | Baylor Football injury surveillance, 2017-2025: season change in injury count and severity, position risk thresholds, Five Pillars prevention proposal. Own `AGENTS.md` + `docs/STATUS.md`. Git repo, pushed to erash11. Disk is the source of truth; the Claude cloud project `Injury Surveillance` is only a pointer. **`data/` holds athlete-identifiable health data — never paste into chat or any external service; gitignored.** |\nPERFORMANCE.md:29:| `AT_Utilization_Benchmarks/` | Athletic training utilization benchmarks → own `CLAUDE.md` |\nPERFORMANCE.md:35:| `S2_Evaluation/` | S2 Cognition evaluation → own `CLAUDE.md`; disk is the source of truth, the Claude cloud project is only a pointer. Program docs in `docs/program/`. Norms and threshold traps: `project_s2-cognition-analysis.md`. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:37:| `CATES/` | Comprehensive Athletic Talent Evaluation System: four-pillar athlete and recruit evaluation, medical A-F grade layered over the weighted score, plus the executive ROI white paper. Own `CLAUDE.md` + `AGENTS.md` + `docs/STATUS.md`. Git repo, pushed to erash11. Disk is the source of truth; the Claude cloud project `Athlete Evaluation Framework` is only a pointer. Program docs in `docs/program/`. No athlete data in the repo: it goes to the primary storage drive, see `data/README.md`. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:40:| `Jump_Dash/` | CMJ jump dashboard for coaching staff (Streamlit, `cmj-dashboard-streamlit/`). Own `AGENTS.md` + `docs/STATUS.md`. Git repo, pushed to erash11. Disk is the source of truth; the Claude cloud project `WebApps` is only a pointer. |\nPERFORMANCE.md:41:| `Ath_Medicine/` | Athletic medicine → own `CLAUDE.md` |\nPERFORMANCE.md:42:| `RTP_ProgressReport/` | Force plate return-to-play progress reports for individual athletes; three report styles, JSX/HTML template rendered per athle…\n\n### memsearch queries\n# memsearch queries\n\n$ for q in 'NCAA webinar data technology best practices continuity plan' 'NCAA attestation report' 'Toby Brooks curriculum' 'Return to Performance course Joe session builder' 'HPI protocol manual Kenny'; do echo \"=== $q\"; memsearch search \"$q\" --top-k 5 2>&1 | head -60; done\n\n/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/.ctx-mode-yXyFzs/script.sh:2: parse error near `for'\n\n### memory files rtp tech ath\n`DEV/RTP_Constraints_Course` — a return-to-play course built on constraints-led\npractice design, sourced from Myszka et al., *Enhancing Skill*.\n\n**Ingest state (as of 2026-09-05): DONE.** 84 atomized advisor entries live in a\nnew SecondBrain vault domain:\n`Knowledge/library/skill-acquisition/enhancing-skill--myszka/`.\n\n**Page facts — do not re-derive these.**\n- Phone scans on disk cover printed pages p001–p253.\n- The PDF was rebuilt on 2026-09-10 and holds printed p001–p253.\n- PDF page N equals printed page N. The offset is **0**.\n- Ordering was verified five separate ways, including against the book's own\n  printed contents page, then verified again after the rebuild.\n  See [[book-scan-page-ordering]].\n\n**Deliberate limit.** Printed pages 254 onward are a blank verso and About the\nAuthors. Eric chose not to scan them because they add no course material.\n\n**Also open:**\n- Import `sources/myszka-references-new.ris` (122 records) into Zotero via\n  File → Import.\n- Write lesson 0002.\n\nBefore any further expensive atomization here, apply the arithmetic gate in\n[[ingest-review-gate]].\n\n## HPI protocol manual\n\n### SB grep keyword files (1)\n# SB grep keyword files\n\n$ cd ~/SecondBrain && for k in 'NCAA' 'attestation' 'continuity' 'Tech Inventory|tech inventory|Tech_Inventory' 'Toby' 'curriculum|Curriculum' 'Return to Performance|return to performance|RTP' 'protocol manual|Create the Manual|HPI protocol' 'Staged to Fall|staged to fall' 'Fall OKR|fall OKR'; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -rlE \"$k\" --include='*.md' . 2>/dev/null | xargs ls -t 2>/dev/null | head -15; done\n\n### memsearch queries\n# memsearch queries\n\n$ for q in 'NCAA webinar data technology best practices continuity plan' 'NCAA attestation report' 'Toby Brooks curriculum' 'Return to Performance course Joe session builder' 'HPI protocol manual Kenny'; do echo \"=== $q\"; memsearch search \"$q\" --top-k 5 2>&1 | head -60; done\n\n/var/folders/gw/8qg6y2bj7rvdqzttmxfl9lx00000gn/T/.ctx-mode-yXyFzs/script.sh:2: parse error near `for'\n\n### DEV area index greps (1)\n# DEV area index greps\n\n$ cd ~/DEV && grep -nEi 'inventory|curricul|rtp|return.to|hpi|manual|ncaa|toby|cla' PERFORMANCE.md PROGRAM.md RESEARCH.md PLATFORM.md FOOTBALL.md 2>/dev/null\n\n## Staged to Fall\n\n### SB grep keyword files (1)\n# SB grep keyword files\n\n$ cd ~/SecondBrain && for k in 'NCAA' 'attestation' 'continuity' 'Tech Inventory|tech inventory|Tech_Inventory' 'Toby' 'curriculum|Curriculum' 'Return to Performance|return to performance|RTP' 'protocol manual|Create the Manual|HPI protocol' 'Staged to Fall|staged to fall' 'Fall OKR|fall OKR'; do echo \"== $k\"; grep -rlE \"$k\" --include='*.md' . 2>/dev/null | xargs ls -t 2>/dev/null | head -15; done\n\n### portfolio json matching entries (1)\n# portfolio json matching entries\n\n$ cd ~/DEV/project-triage && python3 -c \" import json,re d=json.load(open('portfolio.json')) print(type(d), list(d.keys()) if isinstance(d,dict) else len(d)) s=json.dumps(d) for k in d if isinstance(d,dict) else []: v=d[k] if isinstance(v,list): for e in v: t=json.dumps(e) if re.search(r'Tech_Inventory|SoftwareTech|Curriculum|RTP|Return|HPI|Manual|NCAA|Staged|Fall',t,re.I): print('---',k); print(json.dumps(e,indent=1)[:2500]) \"\n\n### memory files rtp tech ath\nThe twice-monthly status report to Chris Ruf (cc Kenny Boyd) is specified by **KR 4.1**\nin `SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md` — five sections\n(Shipped / In Progress / Decisions Needed / Risks–No-Surprises / Next Two Weeks),\nunder 300 words. Built by the `status-report` skill; template at\n`SecondBrain/Templates/status-report.md`.\n\n**Source rules that matter:**\n\n- **\"Shipped\" comes only from `SecondBrain/output/_ledger.md`** — never from\n  `portfolio.json` `stage`. The registry marks projects shipped that still have\n  stakeholder sign-off outstanding (Sport_Tech_Vetting was `shipped` while KR 1.2 showed\n  Chris's sign-off pending). Reporting that to a supervisor claims approval that doesn't\n  exist. Portfolio `stage` feeds \"In Progress\" only.\n- **Read the OKR doc (v3, 14 KRs), never the cadence doc's KR table** — that one is the\n  superseded v2 set of 9 and will produce wrong facts.\n- **`portfolio.json` mixes personal tooling with departmental work.** Filter\n  `lane == \"job\"`. Canonical reportable list lives at\n  `SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md`.\n- **Only 4 of 14 job-lane projects ladder to a KR**, and 10 of 14 KRs have no project.\n  The registry and the OKRs track different halves of the job; neither alone gives an\n  accurate picture.\n\n**Why the report exists:** primarily alignment, secondarily credit — specifically for\ninvolvement with sports beyond football and basketball. The sport tags and the PDF's\ncoverage panel are the mechanism, not decoration. Do not pad the coverage panel; a thin\none is real information and padding destroys the evidentiary value of the honest ones.\n\nRelated: [[fireflies-cli-broken-on-mac]]\n\n\n> **Tip:** Results are scoped to this batch only. To search across all indexed sources, use `ctx_search(queries: [...])` or call ctx_batch_execute with `query_scope: \"global\"`.\n\nSearchable terms for follow-up: 2026-08-19_applied_performance__fall_ops__tech_inventory, 2026-08-24_athletics_all_staff__personnel__software_inventory, 2026-08-27_applied_performance__job_profiles_fms__logistics, 2026-09-03_joe_cla_coursedesign, 2026-09-09_ncaa_ssi_webinar__performance_tech__data_governance, 2026-09-10_sep_10_0937_am, 2026-09-14_team_sync__hiring_process_its__tb_updates, tech_inventory_findings_er_2026-08-29, sport_tech_vetting, ncaa_bestpractices_doc, database_gps_reporting, playerprofiles_fb_03-28-2026, rtp_datacollection_talk, rtp_constraints_course, ncaa_performancetech_v3, 02_sports, _ledger, tech_inventory, tech_inventory_analysis, softwaretech_mgmt_framework, cpss_baylorsportscience_curriculum, status-reports, kristinarash, 2026-08-14-status, 2026-09-07-status, 2026-07-28-interview, 2026-09-09-interview, ai-agent-mastermind-cohort-april-2026, baylor-athletics-leadership, remarkable-extraction-checklist, jd-clarifying-questions, jd-feedback-memo-2026-07-20, jd-response-deliverable-2026-07-20, skill-acquisition, enhancing-skill--myszka, graphify-out, softwaretech, non-responding, deliverables, technologies"}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cc7f7656-e975-4915-84e8-ced6739adbfb","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
