bution now, website as the Fall upgrade.*\n\n**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**\n| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | **Engine launched — 2 issues shipped**: Issue #1 ~Aug 1 anchored by the sleep education module; Issue #2 ~Aug 22 anchored by the GLP-1/performance brief. Proof-of-concept to Chris + stakeholders the week before Issue #1 with a stated ship date. | Eric | 2 issues by Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n| 2.2 | **Both leadership-requested modules circulated** — sleep education + GLP-1 brief in named stakeholders' hands for feedback (the initiative signal the Jul 9 meeting asked for). | Eric | Circulated by Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n| 2.3 | **Reach + demand baseline** — distribution counts recorded at each issue; inbound requests tracked. Targets set from evidence at the Aug 31 review, not guessed now. | Eric | Baseline recorded | ⬜ |\n\n**Staged to Fall:** cadence set from evidence (monthly floor); website distribution; staff/athlete live-session targets; AP Clinic contributions as directed by Courteney (she owns the event — Eric assists).\n\n## Objective 3 — Research & Development\n> **A real R&D engine — committee, repository, formalized partners — that produces publishable output and visibly feeds Baylor's R1 strategy.**\n\n**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**\n| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | **BAIR Steering Committee organized** — vetting process documented, first meeting scheduled with agenda. | Eric | By Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n| 3.2 | **Research repository MVP live** — catalog of projects, status, data, partners. | Eric | By Jul 31 (score honestly at review if late) | ⬜ |\n| 3.3 | **≥1 academic partnership formalized** — named project, written scope + timeline. | Eric | By Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n| 3.4 | **White paper drafted** — converted from the existing short report. Eric sole owner of the critical path; Blake credited as co-author, zero dependency on post-departure contributions (decision 0005). Publication deployment = Fall. | Eric | Drafted by Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n\n## Objective 4 — Leadership & Visibility (enabling)\n> **The director model demonstrably works: staff own their lanes, leadership is never surprised, and the department's work is visible without being asked for.**\n\n**Summer close-out KRs (through Aug 31)**\n| # | Key result | Owner | Target | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 4.1 | **Friday report cadence live** — biweekly email to Chris: Shipped / In Progress / Decisions Needed / Risks–No-Surprises / Next Two Weeks, <300 words. The decision-impact log feeds \"Shipped\" (it is no longer a standalone KR — it's ammunition). | Eric | ≥3 sent by Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n| 4.2 | **AJ full handoff through fall camp** — AJ owns camp planning and the plan-vs-actual review to the football staff (framework already jointly presented); Eric reviews all artifacts pre-delivery, weekly 1:1 standing (decision 0004). | AJ, Eric oversight | 100% of camp practices on framework; review delivered ≤1 wk post-camp | ⬜ |\n| 4.3 | **Noah mentoring cadence** — onboarding checklist written; weekly 1:1; departmental policies/procedures walked through. | Eric | Checklist + cadence live by Aug 15 | ⬜ |\n| 4.4 | **Proactive supervisor meetings held** — Kenny (HPI/research walkthrough) + H&W technology guidance, both initiated by Eric. | Eric | Both held by Aug 31 | ⬜ |\n\n---\n\n## Aug 31 review (cycle close)\nScore each KR 0.0–1.0, keep/retire/add, then author the **Fall (Sep–Dec) set** — first semester cycle, mid-semester checkpoint ~Oct 15. Set education reach targets and newsletter cadence from actuals. Fall candidates already staged: continuity plan, white-paper publication, website distribution, Linda's role integration (pending the Chris conversation), data-management system build.\n\n## Parking lot\n- White paper **published** — Fall.\n- Peer-reviewed submission — the longer-horizon outcome behind the white papers.\n- Year-end research summary — Spring close.\n- Website-based education hub (with Cody) — Fall distribution upgrade.\n\n## Superseded (v2 → v3, 2026-07-17)\n- ~~Unified single dashboard across programs~~ → per-sport on shared data standards (0008).\n- ~~6 newsletter issues / twice-monthly~~ → launch-first reset, 2 module-anchored issues (0006).\n- ~~Quarterly KR cycles~~ → semester cycles + mid-semester checkpoints (0007).\n- ~~Eric delivers fall-camp framework + Aranda review~~ → AJ owns, Eric oversees (0004).\n- ~~Decision-impact log as KR 1.3~~ → fuel for the Friday report (not scored separately).\n- ~~Blake as unit member / KR co-owner~~ → departed; ownership redistributed (0003).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b38f3328-3c89-4bab-ad51-9fa5f71c1d19","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"f33d97a6-e20b-4383-be70-68e1fe6c56e9","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4MFzeJdGoWT9PC7GHZY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QzpaBYJpAdWJnefExnGWqa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat ~/SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md; for p in NCAA_BestPractices_Doc RTP_Constraints_Course Tech_Inventory_Analysis SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum Education_Alignment_Initiative Education_Content_Agent Intern_Curriculum; do echo \"######## $p STATUS\"; head -c 3500 ~/DEV/$p/docs/STATUS.md; echo; done","description":"Read active projects list and project STATUS files"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15266,"cache_read_input_tokens":77989,"output_tokens":910,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":97},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15266},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":77989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15266,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QzpaBYJpAdWJnefExnGWqa":{"command":"cat ~/SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md; for p in NCAA_BestPractices_Doc RTP_Constraints_Course Tech_Inventory_Analysis SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum Education_Alignment_Initiative Education_Content_Agent Intern_Curriculum; do echo \"######## $p STATUS\"; head -c 3500 ~/DEV/$p/docs/STATUS.md; echo; done","description":"Read active projects list and project STATUS files"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cf4MFymTkxC6dr157UTA4","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","attributionMcpServer":"plugin:context-mode:context-mode","attributionMcpTool":"ctx_execute","type":"assistant","uuid":"536a7fdc-1030-45c0-92c6-960e632035ac","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:23:02.126Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"536a7fdc-1030-45c0-92c6-960e632035ac","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QzpaBYJpAdWJnefExnGWqa","type":"tool_result","content":"---\ntype: canonical-list\nowner: Eric Rash\npurpose: The reportable active-project spine. Filters personal tooling out and maps every project to a Key Result and a sport.\nauthority: Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md (v3, 14 KRs)\nsource_registry: /Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage/portfolio.json (lane == \"job\")\nmaintained_by: status-report skill\nupdated: 2026-08-11\n---\n\n# Applied Performance — Canonical Active Projects\n\nThis is the reportable list. It exists because `portfolio.json` mixes personal tooling\n(KeystoneOS, Project_Triage, TSSHB_Skills) with departmental work, and because a project\nwith no Key Result and no sport is hard to justify in a status report.\n\nTwo columns do the work here. **KR** answers *\"why is this on my desk?\"* — a project with\nno KR is either serving an unstated priority or shouldn't be active. **Sport** answers\n*\"who does this help?\"* — and it is the field that makes non-football, non-basketball\ninvolvement visible, which is the reason the status report exists at all.\n\nSeeded 2026-08-11 from the 14 job-lane registry entries. **Sport values marked `TBD` and\nKR mappings marked `?` need your confirmation** — I mapped what the OKR doc states\nexplicitly and refused to guess the rest.\n\n## Reportable\n\n| Project | KR | Sport | Stage | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Coach_Report | 1.1 | Football | shipped | Post-session coach report; mirrors AJ's team report. Eric's protected one-off lane. |\n| Kinexon_Volleyball | 1.1 | Volleyball | building | Eric direct. The volleyball half of KR 1.1's two-sport dashboard target. |\n| Sport_Tech_Vetting | 1.2 | Dept-wide | building | ⚠️ Registry says `shipped`; KR 1.2 says Chris's written sign-off is **outstanding**. Do not report as shipped until sign-off lands. |\n| ForcePlate_DecisionSystem | 1.3 ? | TBD | building | Ladders to HPI dashboarding *if* that's what the redesign serves. Confirm. |\n| SportScienceResearchRepo | 3.2 | Dept-wide | building | ⚠️ KR 3.2 was due **Jul 31** — already past due. Score honestly at the gate. |\n| SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework | — | Dept-wide | building | **Orphan, and the loudest one.** Kenny whiteboard 08-03, stakeholder presentation 08-10 with John Allen and Micah. Active, Kenny-facing, no KR. Either it earns a KR at the Aug 31 gate or it's absorbing time no objective claims. |\n| Transformative_Athlete_Experience | — | Dept-wide | spec | Orphan. Next action is Kenny sign-off. Feeds 4.4 in spirit, isn't 4.4. |\n| PlayerProfiles_FB | — | Football | planned | Orphan by KR, but sits in Eric's protected one-off report lane. Legitimate. |\n| SPA_Presentation | — | TBD | idea | Orphan. From the 2026-07-30 Chris Ruf meeting. |\n| Ask_The_Library | — | Dept-wide | building | Orphan. Health & Performance Evidence Library — adjacent to Objectives 2 and 3, named in neither. |\n| Risk_Stratification_Engine | — | TBD | building | Orphan. Research prototype; no R&D KR covers it. Present as research — no readiness claims. |\n| Travel_Map | — | TBD | building | Orphan. |\n| NCAA_BestPractices_Doc | staged | Dept-wide | idea | Staged to Fall under Objective 1, not a live summer KR. |\n| OKRs_2026-27 | meta | Dept-wide | building | The OKR system itself. Governs the 4.x KRs; not reported as a project. |\n\n## Key Results with no project attached\n\n**10 of 14.** Objectives 2 and 4 are entirely invisible to the registry while the\nregistry's build-heavy work is largely invisible to the OKRs. Worth naming plainly: the\ntwo systems are tracking different halves of the job, and neither one alone would give\nChris an accurate picture.\n\n| KR | What it needs | Due |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | Education engine launched — 2 issues (sleep module, GLP-1 brief) | Aug 31 |\n| 2.2 | Both leadership-requested modules circulated | Aug 31 |\n| 2.3 | Reach + demand baseline recorded | Aug 31 |\n| 3.1 | BAIR Steering Committee organized, first meeting scheduled | Aug 31 |\n| 3.3 | ≥1 academic partnership formalized | Aug 31 |\n| 3.4 | White paper drafted | Aug 31 |\n| 4.1 | **This report — ≥3 sent** | Aug 31 |\n| 4.2 | AJ full handoff through fall camp | post-camp |\n| 4.3 | Noah mentoring cadence live | **Aug 15** |\n| 4.4 | Proactive Kenny + H&W technology meetings held | Aug 31 |\n\n## Sport coverage — the honest baseline\n\nThe report exists to make involvement across sports visible. The roster of programs\ncomes from `DEV/AppliedUtilization/Applied_Performance_Utilization_Brief.md`\n§\"Recommendations by program\" — 15 rows covering all 17 varsity programs. That document\nis **prescriptive** (what each program *could* use), not a record of activity. Measured\nagainst evidence, here is where things actually stand:\n\n| | Programs |\n|---|---|\n| **Named in a project** | Football, Volleyball |\n| **Named in the OKRs** | Football (via AJ), Volleyball (direct) — KR 1.1, and no others |\n| **Appearing in meeting filenames** | Football (11), Baseball (5), Volleyball (3), Softball (2), Acro & Tumbling (2), Tennis (1), Women's Golf (1) |\n| **Zero evidence anywhere** | Men's Basketball, Women's Basketball, Soccer, Men's/Women's XC & Track, Equestrian, Men's Golf, Men's/Women's Tennis as distinct programs |\n\nTwo findings worth sitting with before the first report goes out:\n\n**Both basketball programs have zero recorded activity** — no meetings, no projects — yet\nthey carry detailed recommendations in the utilization brief. That is the largest single\ngap between what the department says it offers and what it demonstrably delivers.\n\n**Soccer is the brief's own \"highest ROI now\" pick** and its best-fit GPS use case, with\nzero meetings and zero projects against it. If the ask driving this report is broader\ninvolvement beyond football and basketball, soccer is the cheapest, best-documented\nplace to start — the case for it is already written in your own brief.\n\nAlso note: `RTP` (24 meetings) and `StaffMeet` (29) dwarf every individual sport in the\ncorpus, but no document lists them as served groups. Real work is happening in lanes\nnone of your planning documents describe, which is its own kind of invisibility.\n\nFour projects carry `TBD` sports. If any of them serve a program outside football and\nvolleyball, that involvement is currently invisible in every system you have — which\nmeans it is invisible to Chris and Kenny too.\n\n## Maintenance\n\nThe `status-report` skill updates stage, sport, and \"moved this period\" on each run. Add\nand retire projects at the Aug 31 gate alongside the KR keep/retire/add pass, so this\nlist and the OKR set stay in step rather than drifting apart the way the registry and\nthe OKRs already have.\n######## NCAA_BestPractices_Doc STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-\n\n######## RTP_Constraints_Course STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Current state\n- The Myszka book has printed pages 1–253 in one verified PDF.\n- PDF page numbers match printed page numbers.\n- All 10 chapters already have 84 library entries.\n\n## Next\n- Import `sources/myszka-references-new.ris` into Zotero.\n- Write lesson 0002.\n\n## Open questions\n- None.\n\n## Gotchas\n- Keep the book PDF and OCR text local and ignored by Git.\n- Do not scan pages 254 onward. They add no course material.\n- Do not run a second book ingest.\n\n######## Tech_Inventory_Analysis STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n\n## Next\n- \n\n## Open questions\n- \n\n######## SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Mac vs Windows copies of the deliverables (checked 2026-09-09)\n\nThree files exist in two versions after the GitHub consolidation. Both kept on\npurpose — do not \"clean up\" one without reading this.\n\n**`Software_and_Technology_Management_Framework_DRAFT.edited_ER`**\n- Text is **identical**: 178 paragraphs each, no tracked changes, no comments.\n- The only real difference is the embedded diagram `word/media/image1.png`:\n  - `...edited_ER.docx` (Mac, 387 KB) — image 1822 x 2350\n  - `...edited_ER_WINDOWS-COPY.docx` (995 KB) — image **3060 x 4980**\n- The Windows copy has the higher-resolution diagram. **Use it for anything\n  printed or projected.** The Mac copy was downscaled at some point.\n- The rest of the size gap is Word housekeeping (empty footnotes/endnotes parts).\n\n**`Technology_Evaluation_Scorecard`** — 38 KB both sides, near identical.\n\n**`Workflow_Diagram.excalidraw`** — compared 2026-09-09: the two files are the\n**same drawing**. 60 elements each, all 60 element ids shared, no element moved,\nidentical 23 text labels. Both re-serialise to exactly 35,586 bytes of content —\nthe 2.5 KB file-size gap is pure indentation whitespace. `_WINDOWS-COPY` is\nredundant and can be dropped at any time. (Note: bigger did NOT mean more\ncontent here, unlike the .docx pair above.)\n\nDecision 2026-09-09: leave all three pairs in place as they are.\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-\n\n######## CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n---\n\n## Merged from windows copy (2026-09-11)\n\n<!-- Contents of STATUS.md.from-windows, kept verbatim so nothing is lost. Fold into the sections above when convenient. -->\n\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-\n\n######## Education_Alignment_Initiative STATUS\n# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- 2026-09-11: Cloud project docs migrated to disk. All 13 .docx docs from the\n  \"Education_Initative\" Claude project are now markdown in `docs/program/`. The cloud\n  project holds only `claude/source-of-truth.md` pointing here.\n- Framework is at capstone stage. Anchor docs: Strategic Alignment Framework,\n  Performance Education Strategic Plan (Updated), EAI Integration Guide.\n\n## Next\n- Decide whether the three Education Czar proposals stay as history or get archived.\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n- Originals (.docx/.pdf) stay at the repo root; the markdown in `docs/program/` is the\n  working copy agents should read.\n\n######## Education_Content_Agent STATUS\n# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n\n## Next\n- \n\n## Open questions\n- \n\n######## Intern_Curriculum STATUS\n﻿# STATUS\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Current state\n- Snapshot committed 2026-09-09 during migration to the DEV + GitHub workflow.\n\n## Next\n-\n\n## Open questions\n-\n\n## Gotchas\n-","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2d53db84-a0b3-4e0d-8ef4-