{"parentUuid":"bdfb3a85-797a-4181-b9fc-722ad38422d5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4MGrct8eBQv1ZWuvHPg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BvrwFAjhHv9rKBUjsPas2p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Inbox && sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-13_Data_Technology_Software_Proposal_Meeting.md | head -70; echo \"######## 08-19\"; sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-19_Applied_Performance__Fall_Ops__Tech_Inventory.md | head -60; echo \"######## 08-27\"; sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-27_Applied_Performance__Job_Profiles_FMS__Logistics.md | head -60; echo \"####### 09-07 status\"; cat status-reports/2026-09-07-status.md; echo \"######## 08-14 status grep\"; grep -nEi 'manual|HPI|NCAA|inventory' status-reports/2026-08-14-status.md","description":"Read tech inventory meetings and status reports"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19172,"cache_read_input_tokens":93255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19172,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BvrwFAjhHv9rKBUjsPas2p":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Inbox && sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-13_Data_Technology_Software_Proposal_Meeting.md | head -70; echo \"######## 08-19\"; sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-19_Applied_Performance__Fall_Ops__Tech_Inventory.md | head -60; echo \"######## 08-27\"; sed -n '/## Summary/,$p' meetings/2026-08-27_Applied_Performance__Job_Profiles_FMS__Logistics.md | head -60; echo \"####### 09-07 status\"; cat status-reports/2026-09-07-status.md; echo \"######## 08-14 status grep\"; grep -nEi 'manual|HPI|NCAA|inventory' status-reports/2026-08-14-status.md","description":"Read tech inventory meetings and status reports"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf4MGqnXAV5HgaeqP56tc","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bfeb4432-444e-42ac-b9a0-6c76df8a9270","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:23:19.289Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"bfeb4432-444e-42ac-b9a0-6c76df8a9270","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BvrwFAjhHv9rKBUjsPas2p","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\n\n### Overview\n\n- **System inventory:** 80-90% of platforms known; small legacy systems unknown, causing risks and data duplication issues.  \n- **Data clarity:** Defining data upfront can cut review delays caused by inconsistent definitions and streamline approvals.  \n- **Process standardization:** Single intake with prioritization and checklist needed; 20% of requests bypass business office causing delays.  \n- **Approval workflows:** Business office as financial filter is crucial; lack of coordination and multiple entry points cause inefficiencies.  \n- **Data governance:** Duplicative data and unclear ownership create risk; need to clarify sign-offs and improve internal system awareness.  \n- **Next steps:** Incremental form improvements and refined proposals aim to speed approvals without disrupting current workflows.\n\n### Action Items\n\n\n**Micah**\nReview Eric’s original proposal and develop a counter-proposal focusing on integrating improvements into existing approval workflows without creating parallel processes (27:10)\nDraft simplified tools like a one-page checklist to standardize intake requests for athletics (27:10)\nCoordinate with Jovan and Cody for follow-up discussions about process improvements and expectations for system requests (35:10)\nLead follow-up conversation with Aaron, Carrie, and Cody to identify existing challenges and necessary process adjustments, including examining email intake flows for requests (35:10)\nImplement adding athletics business office to IDEA form auto-notifications for awareness and coordination (30:00)\n\n**Cody**\nCollaborate internally to manage workflows that screen and clarify requests before IT submission, emphasizing financial feasibility and internal vetting (15:00)\nProvide feedback on proposed process refinements from Micah and support enforcement of standardized intake procedures (27:10)\n\n**Jovan**\nAssist Micah and Cody in review and internal debrief on proposed intake and approval processes (27:10)\n\n**Aaron**\nProvide additional context and clarifications on current requests (e.g., HIPAA mailbox) during follow-up discussions with Micah and others (29:30)\n\n**Carrie and Kenny**\nParticipate in follow-up meetings to clarify data-related challenges, support data stewardship, and inform standardized intake criteria and processes (35:10)\n\n\n### Keywords\n\nathletics, system inventory, data management, approval process, performance data, intake workflow\n\n\n######## 08-19\n## Summary\n\n### Overview\n\n- **Team Operations:** Training schedules fixed; indoor football space pending approval; lean staffing due to no fellow confirmed.  \n- **Athlete Compliance:** NCAA guidelines followed for athlete return; hot weather requires cautious training ramp-up.  \n- **Visa Compliance:** Key staff reapplying for OPT visa; job title adjusted; strict reporting to Homeland Security ongoing.  \n- **Staff Development:** Professional growth sessions start Sept 2; exam prep and onboarding leadership assigned; media content collaboration active.  \n- **Technology Management:** Department tech audit due Aug 29; facility maintenance led by assigned coaches; platform issues affect media updates.  \n- **Budget Constraints:** Equipment replacement limited by funding; older gear monitored for longevity; centralized ordering streamlines supplies.  \n- **Leadership Vision:** Mission stresses discipline, communication, no excuses; clear staff roles assigned; annual calendar to improve planning.\n\n### Action Items\n\n\n**Eric Rash**\nCoordinate schedule management to avoid facility and sport crossover for September events (04:36)\nFollow up with HR regarding fellow position approval and continue communication on staffing (06:14)\nOversee rollout of interview preparation and professional development series starting September 2nd (09:22)\nAssist Coach Winger with leadership on facility operations and upkeep including encouraging proactive reporting and fixes (16:13)\nManage technology inventory survey coordination and promote staff cooperation by August 29th deadline (19:05)\nFollow up on sticker order status with vendor and coaching staff contacts (21:19)\nSupport office supply ordering process based on collected requests (23:20)\nMonitor equipment replacement needs and budget impact, liaise with potential donors for Olympic sports support (26:36)\n\n**Linda**\nAssist Coach Winger with SCCC exam preparation and lead staff onboarding processes (09:22)\nDevelop women’s tennis performance profile and integrate conditioning tests with coach collaboration (14:11)\n\n**Coach Winger**\nLead facility operations and maintenance oversight, ensure proactive facility management and communication (16:13)\nCommunicate travel plans and coverage needs; coordinate with Eric Rash for coverage on tennis and softball (27:59)\n\n**Coach Cord, Coach Hobby, Coach Silas**\nMonitor facility supplies and small item needs; communicate procurement requirements promptly for orders (24:50)\n\n**All Staff**\nCommunicate well during first weeks for athlete onboarding, compliance completion, and schedule updates (23:20)\nProvide details for hurdles and training equipment needed for ordering (24:50)\n\n\n### Keywords\n\nstudent athlete orientation, NCAA compliance, OPT visa, professional development, facility operations, training schedules\n\n######## 08-27\n## Summary\n\n### Overview\n\n- **Meeting Timing & Engagement:** Rushed presentations and late donor remarks lowered energy; better scheduling needed to boost focus and culture messaging.  \n- **Coach Hoot Tribute:** Honoring Hoot emphasized core values and culture, aiding recruitment and daily value reinforcement.  \n- **NCAA Fifth-Year Eligibility:** Unclear NCAA rules and lawsuits complicate roster decisions; legal uncertainty disrupts recruiting and roster planning.  \n- **Freshmen Stress & Support:** Freshmen face high emotional stress; staff urged to provide patience, presence, and communication strategies to ease transitions.  \n- **Footwear Strategy:** Plan to improve shoe quality with sport-specific metcon models; coaches collecting preferences for orders to optimize safety/performance.  \n- **Team Training Status:** Varied team health and readiness; women’s tennis strong, golf conditioning slow, volleyball prepping for tough opener, baseball rebuilding fitness.  \n- **Staff Development & Operations:** Professional growth sessions and student worker hires underway; emphasis on positive attitudes and smooth event coordination.\n\n### Action Items\n\n\n**All Coaches**\nSend preferences for Metcon shoe models (7 or 10) or indicate no need for footwear per team to Will via Kenny (20:58)\n\n**All Staff**\nUpdate and upload current job profiles, resumes, and certifications to the shared Box folder as requested by Kenny (10:07)\n\n**Coaching Staff**\nPractice patience and positive communication early in the semester; draft but do not send emotional emails to avoid miscommunication (14:29)\nIncrease presence at team events and spaces to build relationships with freshmen and newcomers (16:01)\nPrepare and participate in staff professional development sessions focusing on cover letter and application materials; await schedule communication (34:57)\n\n**Kenny**\nCreate and manage a centralized Box folder for staff job profile documents (10:07)\nCoordinate and map route for Zero Blast event on September 4th, ensuring no interference with team schedules; communicate any potential conflicts (17:45)\n\n**Track and Field Staff**\nComplete all Functional Movement Screen (FMS) tests for newcomers and returning athletes; update records including any pain or flags (33:24)\n\n**Sporting Coaches**\nMonitor and accommodate athletes’ fifth-year eligibility status and roster impacts; coordinate with administration on litigated eligibility cases (08:36)\n\n**Hiring Manager**\nFollow up on hiring two student workers to support track and field department; complete onboarding clearances and scheduling (38:34)\n\n\n### Keywords\n\nmeetings, athlete eligibility, staff communication, training updates, footwear, freshmen integration, professional development\n\n####### 09-07 status\n---\ntype: status-report\nreport_number: 2\nperiod_start: 2026-08-24\nperiod_end: 2026-09-07\nrecipients: [Kenny Boyd, Chris Ruf]\nauthority: Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md (v3) — KR 4.1\ncadence: every two weeks\nnext_send: 2026-09-21\nsent: false\nword_count: 287\nsources_degraded:\n  - \"fireflies action-items list --from 21 --agent returned 11 empty {} objects — broken output, not zero items. Action items recovered from the digest inline instead.\"\n  - \"Vault meeting files in period have empty '## Key topics / Decisions / Action items' header blocks — content came from the live digest.\"\n  - \"Meeting corpus stale: newest meeting 2026-09-03. Anything 09-04 to 09-07 comes only from the interview.\"\n  - \"Output ledger has no entries after 2026-08-11 — nothing logged as shipped this period.\"\ninterview_complete: true\n---\n\n# Applied Performance — Status Report #2 (2026-08-24 → 2026-09-07)\n\n## Layer 1 — Email as drafted\n\nSee `2026-09-07-email.txt`. Interview complete 2026-09-07; body is send-ready at 293\nwords. Rename to `2026-09-07-email-sent.txt` and flip `sent: true` after sending.\n\n## Shipped\n\n**Nothing this period.** The output ledger's newest entry is 2026-08-11 (S2 Cognition\noffensive line review). This is an honest zero, not a gap — do not pad it. If the\ninterview surfaces something that shipped and was never logged, append it to\n`output/_ledger.md` first, then add it here.\n\n## In Progress\n\n| Item | Sport | What moved | Next |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Technology / software inventory | Dept-wide | Folded into the department-wide software survey; deadline moved Aug 28 → **Sept 29 soft deadline**. Five units outstanding (Golf M, Tennis, +3). Eric assigned weekly ITS coordination with Michael Lamb (all-staff 08-24) — **Eric unsure 09-07 whether the check-ins have begun**; email says \"setting up,\" not \"started.\" | Chase the five outstanding units before 09-29 |\n| Customer discovery — education | Cross-sport | New workstream out of the 09-02 planning session. Interview ~80% of strength coaches on data needs, readiness questions, cultural support. Two content tracks (short athlete pieces / technical staff sessions). Riverside pilot for video + AI transcription. Website + newsletter as the content hub. Canvas course infrastructure discussed. | Interviews done by late Sept; four videos mid-Oct → early Nov |\n| Functional movement screens | Track & Field | FMS assigned for newcomers and returners (AP staff meeting 08-27). **Ownership unclear** — Eric unsure 09-07 whether this is AP's to report. Cut from the email. | Settle ownership with T&F staff |\n| AP staff meeting cadence | Dept-wide | Every-other-week cadence holding. Noah, AJ, Linda attending. Job profiles + certifications uploaded to Kenny's shared Box folder. | Continue |\n| Return-to-performance course design | Cross-sport | 09-03 session with Joe: individualized progression, session-builder tool concept (reverse calendar progression, drill checklists), ecological dynamics / constraints-led staff education. Jacob (Rehab) approves protocols, Tim (Head AT) on clearance decisions. | Session builder scoping |\n| Perch camera rollout | Football + | **Complete.** Fudge, Simpson and Foster all live. Confirmed by Eric 09-07. | Done |\n| FirstBeat HR monitors | Tennis | **Complete.** Onboarding finished, team using the monitors. Replaced the Polar units. Confirmed by Eric 09-07. | Done |\n| Polar straps + Kinexon integration | Women's Basketball | New this period. WBB integrating Polar straps with Kinexon wearables. **Distinct from the Polar Team System being phased out** — different solution, not a continuation. Confirmed by Eric 09-07. | Scope the integration |\n| ~~Hydration bottles~~ | Football | **Not Applied Performance's** — confirmed by Eric 09-07. Excluded from the email. | — |\n\n## Decisions needed\n\n- **None raised this cycle.** The two open items from report #1 are repeats, not new\n  decisions — see Risks.\n\n## Risks / no surprises\n\n- **REPEAT ASK (2 cycles): SPA meeting time.** Asked in report #1 (08-24), no answer\n  recorded. Skill rule: two unanswered asks means the email has failed at it and it\n  needs raising in person, not a third email line.\n- **REPEAT ASK (2 cycles): Micah follow-up.** Emailed ~08-17, no reply as of 08-24, none\n  logged since. Note: the 08-24 all-staff assigned Eric weekly ITS meetings with Michael\n  Lamb — possibly the same thread resolving through a different door. Verify before\n  re-raising.\n- **OKR cycle close is overdue.** `Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md` v3 runs its\n  summer close-out through **Aug 31**. All 14 KRs still show ⬜ and the Fall (Sep–Dec)\n  set has not been authored. Internal machinery — kept out of the email deliberately.\n- **KR 4.1 missed.** Target was ≥3 reports sent by Aug 31. Actual sends: **1**\n  (2026-08-24). The 2026-08-14 file was drafted, never sent. This report is #2.\n- **VALD MoveHealth+ arriving through a side door (Men's Tennis).** The Men's Tennis\n  consultant wants to use VALD MoveHealth+ to deliver rehab and supplemental training\n  routines. Eric's concern is Kitman EMR integration, and he is chasing it down. This is\n  exactly the case the technology decision matrix (KR 1.2) exists for — a vendor entering\n  via a sport rather than through intake — and KR 1.2 still lacks Chris's written\n  sign-off. Also touches the undecided Kitman vs MyLink question. Raised in the email.\n- **Timing deadline slipped in public.** Report #1 told Kenny and Chris the sur