{"parentUuid":"8f6a1082-ef90-46ef-8eb0-72408b977fca","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019wyjqJKmYBXFcgXKPDhtSY","type":"tool_result","content":"42:| The \"why\" — objectives and Fall KRs | [[Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27]] |\n#### spec\n65:Active (4): Tech Inventory · Education Curriculum · Return to Performance course · HPI protocol manual.\n66:Next up: NCAA best practices for data & technology — takes Tech Inventory's slot when it finishes (assumption, Eric may override).\n73:3. Park all job projects; re-admit the 4 with charters; queue NCAA.\n74:4. Draft Fall KRs from the OKR doc's \"Staged to Fall\" list; Eric confirms.\n#### 07-30 meeting\n2026-07-09_Applied_Performance_Planning_07092026.md\n2026-07-09_CollegeSports_DataPlatform_AMS_Alternatives.md\n2026-07-30_Applied_Performance___Tech_Vetting_Staff_Onboarding__Website.md\n32:- **Performance Data Infrastructure:** Kitman selected for integrated data management aligned with NCAA best practices; flexible guidance preferred over strict policies.\r\n42:Develop an internship curriculum for Noah to incrementally build his experience in applied performance areas, balancing technical learning and administrative coaching (19:01)\r\n47:Initiate discussions or draft best practice processes aligned with NCAA guidelines on systemic infrastructure for performance technology, favoring flexible best practice documents over rigid formal policies (32:15)\r\n53:Engage in communications regarding NCAA best practice policies and coordinate with Eric Rash on policy development approach to align with department goals (32:15)\r\n56:Participate in meetings, learn technology and administration protocols, and assist applied performance staff as part of internship and staff development (14:18)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"072cf063-e8ca-4804-812e-31af126d95d2","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:26:57.819Z","