{"parentUuid":"2abcfe79-c968-4543-bf5f-cd7b63f1d924","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K23TnWchFNnFbCWEoE9PBp","type":"tool_result","content":"#### SWF AGENTS\n### Micah tail\nSeparately, Kenny wants me as the point of contact between Athletics and ITS going\nforward. Would a standing 30 minutes work once this settles? Weekly to start, less as\nit quiets down. Mostly to keep open requests moving and stop the ad hoc ones from\nreaching you cold.\n\nEric\n\nEric Rash\nDirector of Applied Performance | Baylor Athletics\n\n### Humanizer pass — what was removed\n\n- Rule of three: \"settles what data is involved, confirms the rest of Athletics knows\n  about the request, and records who reviewed it here\" → two items\n- Negative parallelism: \"what arrives at your team is better formed, not that there's\n  another step in front of it\"\n- Mild sycophancy: \"That was the most useful part of the meeting for me\"\n- Crafted slogan: \"end up in the same place than cross in the mail\"\n- Flattened the even paragraph rhythm; \"Three questions.\" now stands alone\n\n#### NCAA BP AGENTS\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: NCAA_BestPractices_Doc\n\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7bf5e091-2afb-40f3-98cf-f8f4c0afa7cb","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:27:01.506Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"#### SWF AGENTS\n### Micah tail\nSeparately, Kenny wants me as the point of contact between Athletics and ITS going\nforward. Would a standing 30 minutes work once this settles? Weekly to start, less as\nit quiets down. Mostly to keep open requests moving and stop the ad hoc ones from\nreaching you cold.\n\nEric\n\nEric Rash\nDirector of Applied Performance | Baylor Athletics\n\n### Humanizer pass — what was removed\n\n- Rule of three: \"settles what data is involved, confirms the rest of Athletics knows\n  about the request, and records who reviewed it here\" → two items\n- Negative parallelism: \"what arrives at your team is better formed, not that there's\n  another step in front of it\"\n- Mild sycophancy: \"That was the most useful part of the meeting for me\"\n- Crafted slogan: \"end up in the same place than cross in the mail\"\n- Flattened the even paragraph rhythm; \"Three questions.\" now stands alone\n\n#### NCAA BP AGENTS\n# AGENTS.md\n\nProject: NCAA_BestPractices_Doc\n\n\n## Session routine\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2abcfe79-c968-4543-bf5f-cd7b63f1d924","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
