Care Team Meetings vs. Sport Performance Meetings\n      8.4  Clearance Authority & Procedures\n      8.5  Athlete & Parent Communication Protocols\n9.   Data Repository & Visualization\n      9.1  Data Collection, Storage & Folder Ownership\n      9.2  Athlete Profile Template\n      9.3  Load Monitoring Integration\n      9.4  Reporting & Dashboards\n10.  Forms & Documentation\n      10.1 Testing Record Form\n      10.2 Clearance Sign-Off Form\n11.  Audit, Review & Continuous Improvement\n12.  References & Literature Citations\n13.  Appendices\n      A: NCAA Performance Technology Best Practices\n      B: Rollout Timeline & Communication Plan\n      C: Sport-Specific Normative Data Tables\n      D: Glossary of Terms\n      E: Multi-Format Deliverables Plan","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d87679d5-3370-4d47-aa65-44eb03c00771","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:27:53.120Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"9\nData Repository & Visualization\nEric Rash\n-\n10\nForms & Documentation\nJB\n-\n11\nAudit, Review & Continuous Improvement\nEric Rash\n-\n12\nReferences & Literature Citations\nJeremy\n-\n13\nAppendices\nVarious\n-\nApp. D\nGlossary of Terms\nJacob/Josh\n-\n[Note: Sections 3, 4, and 5 are largely complete based on existing rehab progression and classification documents. Primary work remaining is gathering literature sources (Sections 6-7), writing SOPs (\nTable of Contents\n1.   Executive Summary\n2.   Purpose Statement\n3.   Return-to-Performance (RTP) Protocol Framework\n      3.1  Stage Overview\n      3.2  Injury Classification & Tiered Response\n      3.3  Workload Reintegration Guidelines\n4.   Lower Body RTP Protocol\n      4.1  Testing Battery\n      4.2  Rehabilitation Progression & Decision Framework\n5.   Upper Body RTP Protocol\n      5.1  Testing Battery\n      5.2  Rehabilitation Progression & Decision Framework\n      5.3  Sport-Specific Pathways (Throwing, Contact, Overhead)\n6.   Testing Program\n      6.1  Purpose Statement & Justification\n      6.2  Literatu