{"parentUuid":"4c48d284-c6d1-4161-9680-f5298d3112ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNBNT2sZfXhWL4p5gEbW2D","type":"tool_result","content":"# CONTEXT — JD Role Language Glossary\n\nUbiquitous language for the 2026 Athletics Performance Staff Responsibilities document (Eric Rash, Director of Applied Performance) and the OKR docs built on it. Companion decisions: [[decisions]].\n\n## Assist\n\nAnother named person owns the function and sets direction; Eric executes what they delegate. Ownership, priorities, and external accountability sit with the owner, not Eric.\n\n> Example: AP Clinic — Courteney Tompkins owns the event; Eric takes his responsibilities from her lead. (Resolved 2026-07-16.)\n\n## Oversee (Eric → AP staff)\n\nEric owns the standards, templates, and strategic direction; the staff member owns execution and the external relationships in their lane. Concretely: a weekly 1:1, pre-delivery review of any artifact leaving the department, and no direct involvement in day-to-day operations of the overseen lane.\n\n> Example: AJ owns fall-camp planning and all FB-staff communications, including presenting the plan-vs-actual review to Aranda; Eric reviews artifacts before delivery and co-builds the analysis. (Resolved 2026-07-17.)\n\n## Unified (data & dashboards)\n\nStandardized underneath, bespoke on top. Unification lives in the data layer — common metric definitions, common data model, common freshness expectations — never in a single shared UI. Each sport's dashboards and reports are bespoke deliveries built on that shared foundation.\n\n> Example: KR 1.1 — per-sport coach dashboards (FB via AJ, VB direct) on shared data standards; the HPI protocol and continuity plan are what standardize the underneath. (Resolved 2026-07-17.)\n\n## Support and guide (Eric → BB AP GA)\n\nMentoring-weighted oversight: Eric teaches departmental procedures, policies, and data-management practice; the GA (Noah) executes with training wheels on. Distinct from Oversee — Noah is not yet accountable for a lane's outcomes; Eric is.\n\n## Briefing Asset (department briefing)\n\nThe reusable core content that explains Applied Performance — the three service pillars + capability menu + one-sentence mission — as distinct from any single talk. A **deployment** is one delivery of the asset wrapped for a specific room (audience, ask, and depth vary; the model does not). Deployme\n\n> Example: v1 deployment = the admin/sport-admin briefing; head-coach variant and H&W-onboarding module are staged derivatives, not part of v1. (Resolved 2026-07-18.)\n\n### clarifying Qs head\n# JD Clarifying Questions — Chris Ruf & Kenny Boyd\n\nCompanion to [[JD-feedback-memo-2026-07-20]]. Built from the gaps the 2026-07-17 grilling session exposed: the JD defines lanes but is largely silent on authority, budget, evaluation, and escalation. Questions marked ⇄ are asked of both — triangulate the answers; disagreement between them is itself \n\nAlready resolved elsewhere — do not re-ask: Spirit Squad scope, AP Clinic ownership (Courteney), AJ fall-camp handoff, PD/travel blanks (first offer in memo), Linda (memo names it; live conversation scheduled).\n\n---\n\n## For Chris (direct report — operational clarity)\n\n1. **Success definition ⇄** — When you evaluate me against this document at year's end, what are the two or three things that will matter most to you?\n2. **Technology authority** — \"Vetting, vendor relations, onboarding\": do I own the decision within some threshold, or do I make the recommendation and you approve? Is there a dollar line where it changes?\n3. **Staff oversight depth** — For AJ and Noah, does \"administrative oversight\" include input on hiring, performance reviews, and corrective conversations — or is that your line and I manage the day-to-day only? Who writes their evaluations?\n4. **Standards vs. sport autonomy** — When AJ's football-specific call conflicts with a department standard I've set, whose call wins, and how do you want it escalated — or do you want it to never reach you?\n5. **H&W guidance** — Is my \"guidance to H&W staff on technology and data\" advisory, or does it carry any expectation they follow it? What's my move when guidance is ignored?\n6. **Budget** — Is there an Applied Performance budget line I control (technology, education materials, PD), or does every spend route through you case-by-case?\n7. **Noah's position** — When his GA term ends, is the BB AP position permanent, renewable, mine to backfill — or does it disappear?\n8. **Priority order ⇄** — If the fall forces trade-offs among the HPI build, the education engine, and research infrastructure, what order do you want them protected in?\n9. **Upward reporting** — What do Kenny or Mack ask you about that my Friday reports should be feeding you answers to?\n10. **The stop-doing list** — What have I been doing that this document intends me to stop, hand off, or stay out of? (The document says what I own; I want to hear what I no longer do.)\n### JD source doc on disk","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"70249be1-c635-401a-96b8-66793d8befcc","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:28:10.607Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# CONTEXT — JD Role Language Glossary\n\nUbiquitous language for the 2026 Athletics Performance Staff Responsibilities document (Eric Rash, Director of Applied Performance) and the OKR docs built on it. Companion decisions: [[decisions]].\n\n## Assist\n\nAnother named person owns the function and sets direction; Eric executes what they delegate. Ownership, priorities, and external accountability sit with the owner, not Eric.\n\n> Example: AP Clinic — Courteney Tompkins owns the event; Eric takes his responsibilities from her lead. (Resolved 2026-07-16.)\n\n## Oversee (Eric → AP staff)\n\nEric owns the standards, templates, and strategic direction; the staff member owns execution and the external relationships in their lane. Concretely: a weekly 1:1, pre-delivery review of any artifact leaving the department, and no direct involvement in day-to-day operations of the overseen lane.\n\n> Example: AJ owns fall-camp planning and all FB-staff communications, including presenting the plan-vs-actual review to Aranda; Eric reviews artifacts before delivery and co-builds the analysis. (Resolved 2026-07-17.)\n\n## Unified (data & dashboards)\n\nStandardized underneath, bespoke on top. Unification lives in the data layer — common metric definitions, common data model, common freshness expectations — never in a single shared UI. Each sport's dashboards and reports are bespoke deliveries built on that shared foundation.\n\n> Example: KR 1.1 — per-sport coach dashboards (FB via AJ, VB direct) on shared data standards; the HPI protocol and continuity plan are what standardize the underneath. (Resolved 2026-07-17.)\n\n## Support and guide (Eric → BB AP GA)\n\nMentoring-weighted oversight: Eric teaches departmental procedures, policies, and data-management practice; the GA (Noah) executes with training wheels on. Distinct from Oversee — Noah is not yet accountable for a lane's outcomes; Eric is.\n\n## Briefing Asset (department briefing)\n\nThe reusable core content that explains Applied Performance — the three service pillars + capability menu + one-sentence mission — as distinct from any single talk. A **deployment** is one delivery of the asset wrapped for a specific room (audience, ask, and depth vary; the model does not). Deployme\n\n> Example: v1 deployment = the admin/sport-admin briefing; head-coach variant and H&W-onboarding module are staged derivatives, not part of v1. (Resolved 2026-07-18.)\n\n### clarifying Qs head\n# JD Clarifying Questions — Chris Ruf & Kenny Boyd\n\nCompanion to [[JD-feedback-memo-2026-07-20]]. Built from the gaps the 2026-07-17 grilling session exposed: the JD defines lanes but is largely silent on authority, budget, evaluation, and escalation. Questions marked ⇄ are asked of both — triangulate the answers; disagreement between them is itself \n\nAlready resolved elsewhere — do not re-ask: Spirit Squad scope, AP Clinic ownership (Courteney), AJ fall-camp handoff, PD/travel blanks (first offer in memo), Linda (memo names it; live conversation scheduled).\n\n---\n\n## For Chris (direct report — operational clarity)\n\n1. **Success definition ⇄** — When you evaluate me against this document at year's end, what are the two or three things that will matter most to you?\n2. **Technology authority** — \"Vetting, vendor relations, onboarding\": do I own the decision within some threshold, or do I make the recommendation and you approve? Is there a dollar line where it changes?\n3. **Staff oversight depth** — For AJ and Noah, does \"administrative oversight\" include input on hiring, performance reviews, and corrective conversations — or is that your line and I manage the day-to-day only? Who writes their evaluations?\n4. **Standards vs. sport autonomy** — When AJ's football-specific call conflicts with a department standard I've set, whose call wins, and how do you want it escalated — or do you want it to never reach you?\n5. **H&W guidance** — Is my \"guidance to H&W staff on technology and data\" advisory, or does it carry any expectation they follow it? What's my move when guidance is ignored?\n6. **Budget** — Is there an Applied Performance budget line I control (technology, education materials, PD), or does every spend route through you case-by-case?\n7. **Noah's position** — When his GA term ends, is the BB AP position permanent, renewable, mine to backfill — or does it disappear?\n8. **Priority order ⇄** — If the fall forces trade-offs among the HPI build, the education engine, and research infrastructure, what order do you want them protected in?\n9. **Upward reporting** — What do Kenny or Mack ask you about that my Friday reports should be feeding you answers to?\n10. **The stop-doing list** — What have I been doing that this document intends me to stop, hand off, or stay out of? (The document says what I own; I want to hear what I no longer do.)\n### JD source doc on disk","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4c48d284-c6d1-4161-9680-f5298d3112ce","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"70249be1-c635-401a-96b8-66793d8befcc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4MeYhjPjAZ4ZADyQ9E5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017vWtSnmNoscHHjYEbbPNVr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings && ls | grep -E '^2026-0[3-6].*RTP'; for f in $(ls | grep -E '^2026-04-(1[0-9])_.*RTP' | head -2); do echo \"######## $f\"; grep -nEi 'manual|june 1|kenny|chris|owner|deadline|rollout|approve' \"$f\" | cut -c1-280 | head -15; done","description":"Find spring RTP meetings about the HPI manual"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3240,"cache_read_input_tokens":159777,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3240,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017vWtSnmNoscHHjYEbbPNVr":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings && ls | grep -E '^2026-0[3-6].*RTP'; for f in $(ls | grep -E '^2026-04-(1[0-9])_.*RTP' | head -2); do echo \"######## $f\"; grep -nEi 'manual|june 1|kenny|chris|owner|deadline|rollout|approve' \"$f\" | cut -c1-280 | head -15; done","description":"Find spring RTP meetings about the HPI manual"}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cf4MeXQ6U6o9jLbG42q3Y","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"acce4500-440d-4bc0-8da3-2b7015f47206","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:28:11.457Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"acce4500-440d-4bc0-8da3-2b7015f47206","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017vWtSnmNoscHHjYEbbPNVr","type":"tool_result","content":"2026-03-04_RTP_03042026.md\n2026-03-18_RTP_03182026.md\n2026-04-01_RTP_04012026.md\n2026-04-08_RTP_04082026.md\n2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md\n2026-04-29_Jeremy__Carrie__Physicals_Day__RTP_Tiers.md\n2026-06-03_RTP_HPI_IntroMeeting.md\n2026-06-16_RTP_DataIntegration_PsychosocialReadiness.md\n######## 2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md\n15:- **Documentation Consolidation:** Refine injury documentation and referral forms for clarity; final manual aims for 99% completion by June 1.  \n19:- **Communication Rollout Plan:** A phased communication plan will engage stakeholders and clarify new procedures, launching in June and August.  \n26:Complete sections 3, 4, 5 of the manual focusing on non-medical content; collaborate on sections 6, 7, 8, 9, and 11 as needed (03:25)\n29:Handle all medical sections of the manual; assist with sections 7 and 8 as needed (03:25)\n35:Coordinate briefing of physicians on manual content before large group presentation; clarify clearance documentation expectations with physicians (07:36)\n38:Prepare infographic or presentation-style documents tailored to coaches, physicians, and teams for manual roll-out (07:36)\n43:**Leadership (Carrie, Kenny, Ivins)**\n47:Standardize form and narrative style for manual for consistency across sections before June 1 target (34:24)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ea26de78-5a83-44cf-8203-f6ab1cf80f0a","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:28:12.765Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"2026-03-04_RTP_03042026.md\n2026-03-18_RTP_03182026.md\n2026-04-01_RTP_04012026.md\n2026-04-08_RTP_04082026.md\n2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md\n2026-04-29_Jeremy__Carrie__Physicals_Day__RTP_Tiers.md\n2026-06-03_RTP_HPI_IntroMeeting.md\n2026-06-16_RTP_DataIntegration_PsychosocialReadiness.md\n######## 2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md\n15:- **Documentation Consolidation:** Refine injury documentation and referral forms for clarity; final manual aims for 99% completion by June 1.  \n19:- **Communication Rollout Plan:** A phased communication plan will engage stakeholders and clarify new procedures, launching in June and August.  \n26:Complete sections 3, 4, 5 of the manual focusing on non-medical content; collaborate on sections 6, 7, 8, 9, and 11 as needed (03:25)\n29:Handle all medical sections of the manual; assist with sections 7 and 8 as needed (03:25)\n35:Coordinate briefing of physicians on manual content before large group presentation; clarify clearance documentation expectations with physicians (07:36)\n38:Prepare infographic or presentation-style documents tailored to coaches, physicians, and teams for manual roll-out (07:36)\n43:**Leadership (Carrie, Kenny, Ivins)**\n47:Standardize form and narrative style for manual for consistency across sections before June 1 target (34:24)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"acce4500-440d-4bc0-8da3-2b7015f47206","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
