{"parentUuid":"5de3b255-d883-460b-86f1-9bc2f011617f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4Mh7KaZpkAQakNH8faT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LvRfwrTmfGsWWFUk918JUG","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Fireflies__fireflies_search","input":{"query":"keyword:\"Toby\" scope:sentences from:2026-08-25 to:2026-09-14 limit:10","format":"text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":168287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1097,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LvRfwrTmfGsWWFUk918JUG":{"query":"keyword:\"Toby\" scope:sentences from:2026-08-25 to:2026-09-14 limit:10","format":"text"}},"apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cf4Mh6RGAZxK2Pug4KNuZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ccbfd5ef-6595-4220-85e2-2927d8347f67","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:30:30.476Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ccbfd5ef-6595-4220-85e2-2927d8347f67","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvRfwrTmfGsWWFUk918JUG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"keyword:\\\"Toby\\\" scope:sentences from:2026-08-25 to:2026-09-14 limit:10\",\n  \"results_count\": 1,\n  \"results\": \"[1] Id: 01M1H9BW9DYB17W2JE2RZGGYMZ\\nTitle: Applied Performance — Customer Discovery & Content Plan\\nDateString: 2026-09-02T14:46:30.341Z\\nDuration: 72.9800033569336\\nOrganizer Email: eric.rash11@gmail.com\\nMeeting Link: No meeting link\\nSummary: Short Summary: The discussion defined an applied performance role centered on service, education, research, analytics, and adaptable resources that coaches can tailor to their sports, rather than direct athlete-facing work. Students are preparing data for a research-ready system, with rapid proof-of-concept development and possible external expertise to support scaling. A “start shipping” mindset was encouraged to overcome perfectionism and generate feedback. Customer discovery will begin with short, semi-structured interviews of strength coaches, followed by engagement with athletic medicine and administrators; participants will represent multiple sports, and AI tools such as Fireflies, Granola, and Decipher will support transcription and analysis. Content will use two tracks: brief social-media clips for athletes and deeper technical sessions for staff. Riverside and similar tools may automate editing, captioning, and publishing. Initial goals include four videos by the end of September, interview analysis afterward, and four additional videos between mid-October and early November. Adoption depends on addressing technology gaps, leadership support, staff buy-in, and cultural development., Keywords: Applied Performance, Customer Discovery, Educational Content, Data-Driven Metrics, Strength Coaches, AI Tools, Action Items: \\n**Eric Rash**\\nDevelop initial customer discovery interview questions tailored for strength coaches and athletic staff by early September (29:19)\\nSchedule and conduct interviews with a representative sample (~80%) of strength coaches focusing on data needs, readiness questions, and cultural support for applied performance (18:36)\\nCollaborate on creating educational content in two tracks: short actionable pieces for athletes and detailed technical sessions for coaches and staff (35:47)\\nPilot content creation using Riverside or similar tool, including video recording, AI transcription, and clipping, with assistance from student assistants (38:15)\\nCoordinate with internal stakeholders (athletic medicine, coaches, administrators) to understand cultural and budgetary constraints affecting adoption of applied performance initiatives (29:19)\\nBuild out mockup applied performance website and newsletter to serve as content hub (01:06:15)\\nPlan and adhere to a timeline: complete interview phase by late September, analyze data with AI tools, then push out four videos by mid-October to early November (01:07:53)\\nContinue education and culture development initiatives beyond preceptorship role to sustain long-term applied performance integration (01:09:28)\\nAttend follow-up meetings scheduled tentatively for Fridays or midweek after 5 pm to maintain project momentum and accountability (01:11:30)\\n\\n**Meeting Organizer/Unknown Speaker**\\nAssist Eric Rash in refining interview scripts based on initial feedback and provide expertise on interview methodology and qualitative data analysis (19:53)\\nProvide guidance on AI tools for transcription and data synthesis, like Fireflies and Granola, and demonstrate video production workflow using Riverside (38:15)\\nSupport content strategy development focusing on actionable, bite-sized educational content and framework for measuring success (58:00)\\nShare insights from past educational programs (Performance School/Academy) and recommend delivery formats to increase engagement (01:02:30)\\nCollaborate on setting up Canvas course infrastructure and safeguarding content access for internal distribution with optional assignments and quizzes (01:04:30)\\nCommit to meeting and interview scheduling support; offer to sit in on interviews and advise on execution plan and accountability (01:07:53)\\n\\nMeeting Attendees: No meeting attendees\\nMeeting Info: Silent Meeting: false, Summary Status: processed\\nParticipants: eric.rash11@gmail.com\"\n}"}]}]},"uuid":"d2f0ad68-b6ed-49e8-9219-2b355e08d85c","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:30:31.655Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"keyword:\\\"Toby\\\" scope:sentences from:2026-08-25 to:2026-09-14 limit:10\",\n  \"results_count\": 1,\n  \"results\": \"[1] Id: 01M1H9BW9DYB17W2JE2RZGGYMZ\\nTitle: Applied Performance — Customer Discovery & Content Plan\\nDateString: 2026-09-02T14:46:30.341Z\\nDuration: 72.9800033569336\\nOrganizer Email: eric.rash11@gmail.com\\nMeeting Link: No meeting link\\nSummary: Short Summary: The discussion defined an applied performance role centered on service, education, research, analytics, and adaptable resources that coaches can tailor to their sports, rather than direct athlete-facing work. Students are preparing data for a research-ready system, with rapid proof-of-concept development and possible external expertise to support scaling. A “start shipping” mindset was encouraged to overcome perfectionism and generate feedback. Customer discovery will begin with short, semi-structured interviews of strength coaches, followed by engagement with athletic medicine and administrators; participants will represent multiple sports, and AI tools such as Fireflies, Granola, and Decipher will support transcription and analysis. Content will use two tracks: brief social-media clips for athletes and deeper technical sessions for staff. Riverside and similar tools may automate editing, captioning, and publishing. Initial goals include four videos by the end of September, interview analysis afterward, and four additional videos between mid-October and early November. Adoption depends on addressing technology gaps, leadership support, staff buy-in, and cultural development., Keywords: Applied Performance, Customer Discovery, Educational Content, Data-Driven Metrics, Strength Coaches, AI Tools, Action Items: \\n**Eric Rash**\\nDevelop initial customer discovery interview questions tailored for strength coaches and athletic staff by early September (29:19)\\nSchedule and conduct interviews with a representative sample (~80%) of strength coaches focusing on data needs, readiness questions, and cultural support for applied performance (18:36)\\nCollaborate on creating educational content in two tracks: short actionable pieces for athletes and detailed technical sessions for coaches and staff (35:47)\\nPilot content creation using Riverside or similar tool, including video recording, AI transcription, and clipping, with assistance from student assistants (38:15)\\nCoordinate with internal stakeholders (athletic medicine, coaches, administrators) to understand cultural and budgetary constraints affecting adoption of applied performance initiatives (29:19)\\nBuild out mockup applied performance website and newsletter to serve as content hub (01:06:15)\\nPlan and adhere to a timeline: complete interview phase by late September, analyze data with AI tools, then push out four videos by mid-October to early November (01:07:53)\\nContinue education and culture development initiatives beyond preceptorship role to sustain long-term applied performance integration (01:09:28)\\nAttend follow-up meetings scheduled tentatively for Fridays or midweek after 5 pm to maintain project momentum and accountability (01:11:30)\\n\\n**Meeting Organizer/Unknown Speaker**\\nAssist Eric Rash in refining interview scripts based on initial feedback and provide expertise on interview methodology and qualitative data analysis (19:53)\\nProvide guidance on AI tools for transcription and data synthesis, like Fireflies and Granola, and demonstrate video production workflow using Riverside (38:15)\\nSupport content strategy development focusing on actionable, bite-sized educational content and framework for measuring success (58:00)\\nShare insights from past educational programs (Performance School/Academy) and recommend delivery formats to increase engagement (01:02:30)\\nCollaborate on setting up Canvas course infrastructure and safeguarding content access for internal distribution with optional assignments and quizzes (01:04:30)\\nCommit to meeting and interview scheduling support; offer to sit in on interviews and advise on execution plan and accountability (01:07:53)\\n\\nMeeting Attendees: No meeting attendees\\nMeeting Info: Silent Meeting: false, Summary Status: processed\\nParticipants: eric.rash11@gmail.com\"\n}"}],"mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"mcp-ff","version":"0.1.0","description":"Fireflies.ai MCP server for meeting transcript access"}}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ccbfd5ef-6595-4220-85e2-2927d8347f67","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"d2f0ad68-b6ed-49e8-9219-2b355e08d85c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4Mh7KaZpkAQakNH8faT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014aMdxSqE5xh9h9htGHkNVh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026 && grep -nEi 'educat|curricul|research|newsletter' JD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md decisions.md | cut -c1-260 | head -14; echo \"### cadence 35-50\"; sed -n 35,50p ../Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md | cut -c1-260; echo \"### spec 55-80\"; sed -n 55,80p ~/DEV/project-triage/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system-design.md | cut -c1-260; echo \"### RTP_WG program grep\"; grep -nEi 'due|deadline|Kenny|Chris|walkthrough|June 1|august' ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/program/*.md ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/README.md | cut -c1-240 | head -14","description":"Grep JD education duties, cadence, spec, RTP working group dates"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1097,"cache_read_input_tokens":168287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1097,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014aMdxSqE5xh9h9htGHkNVh":{"command":"cd ~/SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-JD-2026 && grep -nEi 'educat|curricul|research|newsletter' JD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md decisions.md | cut -c1-260 | head -14; echo \"### cadence 35-50\"; sed -n 35,50p ../Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md | cut -c1-260; echo \"### spec 55-80\"; sed -n 55,80p ~/DEV/project-triage/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system-design.md | cut -c1-260; echo \"### RTP_WG program grep\"; grep -nEi 'due|deadline|Kenny|Chris|walkthrough|June 1|august' ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/program/*.md ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/README.md | cut -c1-240 | head -14","description":"Grep JD education duties, cadence, spec, RTP working group dates"}},"apiBlockIndex":5,"requestId":"req_011Cf4Mh6RGAZxK2Pug4KNuZ","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d6d8bb0-a5f7-4b32-9a68-c37ab111a799","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:30:34.914Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5d6d8bb0-a5f7-4b32-9a68-c37ab111a799","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d23fcdcc-b354-43a5-a06a-e16fcb59f267","agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014aMdxSqE5xh9h9htGHkNVh","type":"tool_result","content":"JD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:22:| 4 | **Budget:** is there an AP budget line I manage for technology, education materials, and PD? | A defined annual line I manage with your visibility, spends over an agreed threshold routed to you. If no line exists,\nJD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:33:| **Aug 1** | Newsletter Issue #1 ships (sleep education module) — proof-of-concept to you and stakeholders the week prior with stated ship date. |\nJD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:36:| **Aug 22** | Newsletter Issue #2 ships (GLP-1/performance brief). |\ndecisions.md:77:## 0006 — Education engine reset: 2 module-anchored issues, launch decoupled from website and from approval\ndecisions.md:83:**Decision:** KR 2.1 resets to 2 issues by Aug 31 — Issue #1 by ~Aug 1 anchored by the sleep education module, Issue #2 by ~Aug 22 anchored by the GLP-1 brief, both modules circulated to named stakeholders. The proof-of-concept goes out advance\ndecisions.md:95:**Context:** Eric proposed replacing quarterly OKR cycles with semester-long ones (Aug–Dec, Jan–May) to match the athletic calendar and the true duration of infrastructure builds. Risk named and accepted: his self-identified failure mode is exe\ndecisions.md:127:**Alternatives considered:** Anchor to a named live decision (makes the KR hostage to an external party's negotiation pace — the exact failure property the newsletter taught); existence-only (repeats the original shelf-ware outcome).\n### cadence 35-50\n- a slot is open and a project is waiting.\n\n## Where things live\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| The project list, charters, cap | `DEV/project-triage/portfolio.json` (`charter` per project, `meta.slate`) |\n| The \"why\" — objectives and Fall KRs | [[Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27]] |\n| Check now | `python3 ~/DEV/project-triage/portfolio.py slate-check` |\n| Pulse to Chris + Kenny | Biweekly status report — Shipped comes from finished steps |\n\n## When a step slips\n\nDo one of three things the same week: **do it**, **re-date it with the receiver** (tell them), or **drop the project** and free the slot. Silent slipping is the only wrong answer.\n\n## Retired\n### spec 55-80\n## Where things live\n\n- **`portfolio.json`** — the one project list (charters, cap, next-up, checkpoints).\n- **`SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md`** — the \"why\": objectives and Fall KRs.\n- **`SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md`** — replaced by a short page of these rules.\n- **Retired:** `SecondBrain/Projects/okr-tracker/` (frozen since 2026-06-12, still the June KR set).\n- **Out of scope:** side-lane projects (CFB, KeystoneOS). Revisit if they keep eating job time.\n\n## Fall 2026 slate (Eric's picks, 2026-09-14)\n\nActive (4): Tech Inventory · Education Curriculum · Return to Performance course · HPI protocol manual.\nNext up: NCAA best practices for data & technology — takes Tech Inventory's slot when it finishes (assumption, Eric may override).\nGap noted: no research-pillar project this semester. Decide on purpose when the Fall KRs are written.\n\n## Build order\n\n1. This doc.\n2. Score the 14 summer KRs with Eric (he gives numbers).\n3. Park all job projects; re-admit the 4 with charters; queue NCAA.\n4. Draft Fall KRs from the OKR doc's \"Staged to Fall\" list; Eric confirms.\n5. `slate-check` + tests; wire into `ritual-check.ps1` + tests.\n### RTP_WG program grep\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/program/rtp-gaps-overview-for-kb.md:3:Baylor Health & Wellness. RTP Working Group 2025-26. Overview prepared for Kenny Boyd.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2b061b55-465e-4a56-978c-a36e5e77dfda","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:30:36.342Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"JD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:22:| 4 | **Budget:** is there an AP budget line I manage for technology, education materials, and PD? | A defined annual line I manage with your visibility, spends over an agreed threshold routed to you. If no line exists,\nJD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:33:| **Aug 1** | Newsletter Issue #1 ships (sleep education module) — proof-of-concept to you and stakeholders the week prior with stated ship date. |\nJD-response-deliverable-2026-07-20.md:36:| **Aug 22** | Newsletter Issue #2 ships (GLP-1/performance brief). |\ndecisions.md:77:## 0006 — Education engine reset: 2 module-anchored issues, launch decoupled from website and from approval\ndecisions.md:83:**Decision:** KR 2.1 resets to 2 issues by Aug 31 — Issue #1 by ~Aug 1 anchored by the sleep education module, Issue #2 by ~Aug 22 anchored by the GLP-1 brief, both modules circulated to named stakeholders. The proof-of-concept goes out advance\ndecisions.md:95:**Context:** Eric proposed replacing quarterly OKR cycles with semester-long ones (Aug–Dec, Jan–May) to match the athletic calendar and the true duration of infrastructure builds. Risk named and accepted: his self-identified failure mode is exe\ndecisions.md:127:**Alternatives considered:** Anchor to a named live decision (makes the KR hostage to an external party's negotiation pace — the exact failure property the newsletter taught); existence-only (repeats the original shelf-ware outcome).\n### cadence 35-50\n- a slot is open and a project is waiting.\n\n## Where things live\n\n| What | Where |\n|---|---|\n| The project list, charters, cap | `DEV/project-triage/portfolio.json` (`charter` per project, `meta.slate`) |\n| The \"why\" — objectives and Fall KRs | [[Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27]] |\n| Check now | `python3 ~/DEV/project-triage/portfolio.py slate-check` |\n| Pulse to Chris + Kenny | Biweekly status report — Shipped comes from finished steps |\n\n## When a step slips\n\nDo one of three things the same week: **do it**, **re-date it with the receiver** (tell them), or **drop the project** and free the slot. Silent slipping is the only wrong answer.\n\n## Retired\n### spec 55-80\n## Where things live\n\n- **`portfolio.json`** — the one project list (charters, cap, next-up, checkpoints).\n- **`SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md`** — the \"why\": objectives and Fall KRs.\n- **`SecondBrain/Projects/Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md`** — replaced by a short page of these rules.\n- **Retired:** `SecondBrain/Projects/okr-tracker/` (frozen since 2026-06-12, still the June KR set).\n- **Out of scope:** side-lane projects (CFB, KeystoneOS). Revisit if they keep eating job time.\n\n## Fall 2026 slate (Eric's picks, 2026-09-14)\n\nActive (4): Tech Inventory · Education Curriculum · Return to Performance course · HPI protocol manual.\nNext up: NCAA best practices for data & technology — takes Tech Inventory's slot when it finishes (assumption, Eric may override).\nGap noted: no research-pillar project this semester. Decide on purpose when the Fall KRs are written.\n\n## Build order\n\n1. This doc.\n2. Score the 14 summer KRs with Eric (he gives numbers).\n3. Park all job projects; re-admit the 4 with charters; queue NCAA.\n4. Draft Fall KRs from the OKR doc's \"Staged to Fall\" list; Eric confirms.\n5. `slate-check` + tests; wire into `ritual-check.ps1` + tests.\n### RTP_WG program grep\n/Users/kristinarash/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/program/rtp-gaps-overview-for-kb.md:3:Baylor Health & Wellness. RTP Working Group 2025-26. Overview prepared for Kenny Boyd.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5d6d8bb0-a5f7-4b32-9a68-c37ab111a799","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
