{"parentUuid":"f5c6d947-d1f1-465a-8ae7-f14beb8e1d7b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4MtfDXz6cGc9wWUGqJ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uh8MkP2VxedWyNvWws91qT","name":"SubagentHandback","input":{"message":"Research only; I edited no files. Paths: SB = ~/SecondBrain, M = SB/Inbox/meetings. Every field I could not find says UNKNOWN.\n\n## 1. Tech Inventory\n- **Portfolio entries:** `Tech_Inventory_Analysis` (job lane, rank 16, building) and `SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework` (rank 12). Folders are ~/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis and ~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework.\n- **Who asked:** Kenny Boyd chaired the 08-13 review and said \"I do think we need to figure out all the systems that we're using\" (quoted in the portfolio update of 08-30). The 08-24 all-staff meeting then assigned it: \"Eric to inventory all departmental software and coordinate increased ITS communication via weekly meetings with Michael Lamb\" (M/2026-08-24_Athletics_All_Staff__Personnel__Software_Inventory.md). The meeting note does not say who led the all-staff meeting.\n- **Receiver:** Kenny, as an inference. The portfolio update (08-30) says \"The inventory IS Kenny's ask\" and that his format is \"the one-page EXEC_SUMMARY docx\". No direct confirmation from Kenny.\n- **Done means:** final EXEC_SUMMARY one-pager, plus FINDINGS rebuilt on final numbers. Current interim versions are on Drive at 05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-09-01_.docx and TechInventory_2026-08/.\n  - Note: Kenny's 08-13 \"one page checklist\" was about the intake worksheet, not the inventory.\n- **Hard date:** department soft deadline 29 Sep 2026, set at the 08-24 meeting.\n- **Outstanding units:** status-log 9/14 says \"Volleyball is the only one outstanding\". The 9/8 reminder had gone to five units (docs/INVENTORY_REMINDER_2026-09-08-sent.md). SCRL app and JABA are still unidentified.\n- **ITS dependency:** status-log 9/14 says \"Micah Lamb — no response on the tech review process, about 4 weeks now\". Micah is writing a counter-proposal (MEETING_RECORD_2026-08-13).\n- **JD duty wording:** UNKNOWN. I could not find the JD source document anywhere.\n\n## 2. Education Curriculum\n- **Not the same as `SportScience_Curriculum`.** That entry is side lane: \"15-16 week sport science curriculum for students\", dev_folder CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum, which is intern curriculum content.\n- **No matching job-lane portfolio entry.** Related folders: Education_Content_Agent, Education_Alignment_Initiative, TechEd_Prop.\n- **Source:** M/2026-09-02_Applied_Performance__Customer_Discovery__Content_Plan.md, Fireflies 01M1H9BW9DYB17W2JE2RZGGYMZ.\n- **The other speaker is Toby Brooks (inferred).** Speaker 1 says \"Toby\" to Speaker 2, and Speaker 2 mentions \"I've got to get these hundred hours\" and \"well beyond preceptorship\". So Toby is a practicum student and collaborator, not a receiver.\n- **Who asked / receiver:** UNKNOWN. Toby only offered help (scripts, Canvas \"shell… enroll by team\").\n- **Pillar:** Education (OKR Objective 2). The status log of 9/14 says \"Going to meet with Toby Brooks to help build out the education curriculum\".\n- **Dates stated:**\n  - Interviews with about 80% of strength coaches, done \"by late September\".\n  - Four videos: Eric said \"by end of September… four videos\". Toby then proposed \"mid October to early November, push out four videos\". The summary lists both, so the two conflict.\n  - A website/newsletter mock-up and a Canvas course were discussed, with no dates.\n- **Done means:** UNKNOWN.\n\n## 3. Return to Performance course\n- **Same thing as the RTP CLA course.** Folder ~/DEV/RTP_Constraints_Course; PROGRAM.md row \"for Joe Smith, plus a planned drill-design tool\". Listed in the portfolio only as an 08-18 inbox idea: \"Course-builder agent… to walk AT Joe Smith through\".\n- **Learner/receiver:** Joe Smith, assistant athletic trainer. He is not Joe Reed, the Men's Tennis consultant. CLAUDE.md says \"Sponsor: Eric Rash\".\n- **Who asked:** self-started by Eric. MISSION.md was \"Confirmed with Joe on 2026-09-03\": \"I want to be known as the guy… that does return to performance\".\n- **Gatekeepers:** \"Jacob (director of rehab) and Tim (head athletic trainer)\" (MISSION.md:58; M/2026-09-03_Joe_CLA_CourseDesign.md).\n- **Existing work:**\n  - lessons/0001-opposed-vs-unopposed.html, shipped 09-03\n  - 84 library entries from the Myszka book\n  - Next steps (docs/STATUS.md): write lesson 0002 and import the RIS file. The session-builder tool is \"planned\".\n- **Dates / done means:** UNKNOWN. No deadlines are set anywhere.\n\n## 4. HPI protocol manual\n- **KR 1.3** (SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md): \"HPI protocol v1 drafted — data integration, flow, storage, dashboarding, interpretation — circulated to Chris + Kenny… walked through with Kenny\". Due Aug 31; not scored.\n  - **Receiver: Chris Ruf + Kenny Boyd.** Also in JD-feedback-memo-2026-07-20.md:22.\n- **Status:** the 08-14 status report says \"No movement logged\". There are no HPI meetings July–September.\n- **This is one of Eric's JD lanes:** \"HPI protocol and its dashboarding\" (OKR doc). Exact JD wording: UNKNOWN.\n- **A separate existing draft:** ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/HPI_RTP_Manual_Outline_V3.docx (plus V2, ORIGINAL). \"Return-to-Performance Manual… Effective Date: June 1, 2026 | Version 3.0 | Draft\", 13 sections.\n  - Eric owns sections 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11; Jeremy owns 3–5; JB owns 10.\n  - Appendix A is \"NCAA Performance Technology Best Practices\".\n  - The June 1 target has lapsed (source: M/2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md).\n  - KR 1.3 roughly maps to sections 6, 7, 9 and 11. The full manual depends on Jeremy and JB, which breaks the OKR rule \"critical path inside the unit's control\".\n- **\"Create the Manual\":** that phrase appears nowhere.\n- **Hard date / done means:** UNKNOWN beyond the lapsed Aug 31 and June 1 targets.\n\n## 5. NCAA best practices for data & technology\n- **Portfolio:** `NCAA_BestPractices_Doc` (job lane, rank 2, stage idea), \"Chris Ruf meeting deliverable\". It came from M/2026-07-30_Applied_Performance___Tech_Vetting_Staff_Onboarding__Website.md (32:15): \"favoring flexible best practice documents over rigid formal policies\".\n  - The folder ~/DEV/NCAA_BestPractices_Doc has an empty STATUS.\n  - It is \"Staged to Fall\" under Objective 1.\n- **Receiver:** Chris Ruf, as an inference from the portfolio purpose text.\n- **Webinar (2026-09-09, 45 min, NCAA SSI, speakers Tim Coffey and Mark Koberly/Coberly):**\n  - `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings/2026-09-09_NCAA_SSI_Webinar__Performance_Tech__Data_Governance.md` (Fireflies 01M23EEHZ3CRE03AYYADWA3N0D)\n  - `/Users/kristinarash/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/SSI_Notes_09092026.docx` (12 KB of text, dated Sep 10)\n  - No PDF or slides found after 09-05 in Downloads, Documents, Drive or OneDrive.\n- **Recommendations stated:**\n  - A written plan/policy for adopting technology (justification, validity/reliability, data ownership, access)\n  - Consult general counsel, IT and risk management\n  - Routinely re-evaluate whether each tool gives actionable value\n  - Educate staff, coaches and athletes before deploying anything\n  - Get athlete consent, with opt-out where feasible\n  - Collect athlete feedback\n  - Review vendor contracts for data resale\n  - Link medical and performance data\n- **\"Data continuity plan\" is not from the webinar.** It comes from the OKR doc: \"Staged to Fall: data-continuity plan per NCAA Best Practices document (what survives a staff transition)\".\n- **Earlier NCAA material:** Drive 01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/ (Action_Plan, Condensed, SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations, SSI_PerformanceTech_StaffOverview_v3.md) and ~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/deliverables/NCAA_PerformanceTech_v3.docx.\n- **The 9/14 attestation item is unrelated.** It came from the student-services staff meeting (M/2026-09-14_Team_Sync…, 36:40): \"Finalize and circulate NCAA attestation report draft… end of September… submission by mid-October\". It is a student-athlete services compliance report (see M/2026-05-07 mental-health attestation and Drive 06_TEMPLATES/KB_Doc_Examples/NCAA Attestations Information - Baylor Athletics - SA Services - Fall 2025.docx). Nothing ties it to data/tech or to Eric.\n- **Hard date / done means:** UNKNOWN.\n\n## Staged to Fall / Fall OKR drafts\n- The \"Staged to Fall\" lists exist only in SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md, dated 07-17, v3. Its Aug 31 section adds the Fall candidates \"continuity plan, white-paper publication, website distribution, Linda's role integration, data-management system build\". SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md lists NCAA_BestPractices_Doc as \"staged\".\n- **No Fall OKR set has been written.** Status report of 09-07: \"the Fall (Sep–Dec) set has not been authored\".\n- **Only files touched after 08-31:**\n  - SB/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-status.md\n  - SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md (09-14)\n  - ~/DEV/project-triage/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system-design.md (Fall slate and build step \"Draft Fall KRs from… Staged to Fall\")"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_read_input_tokens":179468,"output_tokens":4163,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":119},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":4163,"cache_read_input_tokens":179468,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2076,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Uh8MkP2VxedWyNvWws91qT":{"message":"Research only; I edited no files. Paths: SB = ~/SecondBrain, M = SB/Inbox/meetings. Every field I could not find says UNKNOWN.\n\n## 1. Tech Inventory\n- **Portfolio entries:** `Tech_Inventory_Analysis` (job lane, rank 16, building) and `SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework` (rank 12). Folders are ~/DEV/Tech_Inventory_Analysis and ~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework.\n- **Who asked:** Kenny Boyd chaired the 08-13 review and said \"I do think we need to figure out all the systems that we're using\" (quoted in the portfolio update of 08-30). The 08-24 all-staff meeting then assigned it: \"Eric to inventory all departmental software and coordinate increased ITS communication via weekly meetings with Michael Lamb\" (M/2026-08-24_Athletics_All_Staff__Personnel__Software_Inventory.md). The meeting note does not say who led the all-staff meeting.\n- **Receiver:** Kenny, as an inference. The portfolio update (08-30) says \"The inventory IS Kenny's ask\" and that his format is \"the one-page EXEC_SUMMARY docx\". No direct confirmation from Kenny.\n- **Done means:** final EXEC_SUMMARY one-pager, plus FINDINGS rebuilt on final numbers. Current interim versions are on Drive at 05_SYSTEMS/SoftwareTechDocs/Tech_Inventory_EXEC_SUMMARY_ER_2026-09-01_.docx and TechInventory_2026-08/.\n  - Note: Kenny's 08-13 \"one page checklist\" was about the intake worksheet, not the inventory.\n- **Hard date:** department soft deadline 29 Sep 2026, set at the 08-24 meeting.\n- **Outstanding units:** status-log 9/14 says \"Volleyball is the only one outstanding\". The 9/8 reminder had gone to five units (docs/INVENTORY_REMINDER_2026-09-08-sent.md). SCRL app and JABA are still unidentified.\n- **ITS dependency:** status-log 9/14 says \"Micah Lamb — no response on the tech review process, about 4 weeks now\". Micah is writing a counter-proposal (MEETING_RECORD_2026-08-13).\n- **JD duty wording:** UNKNOWN. I could not find the JD source document anywhere.\n\n## 2. Education Curriculum\n- **Not the same as `SportScience_Curriculum`.** That entry is side lane: \"15-16 week sport science curriculum for students\", dev_folder CPSS_BaylorSportScience_Curriculum, which is intern curriculum content.\n- **No matching job-lane portfolio entry.** Related folders: Education_Content_Agent, Education_Alignment_Initiative, TechEd_Prop.\n- **Source:** M/2026-09-02_Applied_Performance__Customer_Discovery__Content_Plan.md, Fireflies 01M1H9BW9DYB17W2JE2RZGGYMZ.\n- **The other speaker is Toby Brooks (inferred).** Speaker 1 says \"Toby\" to Speaker 2, and Speaker 2 mentions \"I've got to get these hundred hours\" and \"well beyond preceptorship\". So Toby is a practicum student and collaborator, not a receiver.\n- **Who asked / receiver:** UNKNOWN. Toby only offered help (scripts, Canvas \"shell… enroll by team\").\n- **Pillar:** Education (OKR Objective 2). The status log of 9/14 says \"Going to meet with Toby Brooks to help build out the education curriculum\".\n- **Dates stated:**\n  - Interviews with about 80% of strength coaches, done \"by late September\".\n  - Four videos: Eric said \"by end of September… four videos\". Toby then proposed \"mid October to early November, push out four videos\". The summary lists both, so the two conflict.\n  - A website/newsletter mock-up and a Canvas course were discussed, with no dates.\n- **Done means:** UNKNOWN.\n\n## 3. Return to Performance course\n- **Same thing as the RTP CLA course.** Folder ~/DEV/RTP_Constraints_Course; PROGRAM.md row \"for Joe Smith, plus a planned drill-design tool\". Listed in the portfolio only as an 08-18 inbox idea: \"Course-builder agent… to walk AT Joe Smith through\".\n- **Learner/receiver:** Joe Smith, assistant athletic trainer. He is not Joe Reed, the Men's Tennis consultant. CLAUDE.md says \"Sponsor: Eric Rash\".\n- **Who asked:** self-started by Eric. MISSION.md was \"Confirmed with Joe on 2026-09-03\": \"I want to be known as the guy… that does return to performance\".\n- **Gatekeepers:** \"Jacob (director of rehab) and Tim (head athletic trainer)\" (MISSION.md:58; M/2026-09-03_Joe_CLA_CourseDesign.md).\n- **Existing work:**\n  - lessons/0001-opposed-vs-unopposed.html, shipped 09-03\n  - 84 library entries from the Myszka book\n  - Next steps (docs/STATUS.md): write lesson 0002 and import the RIS file. The session-builder tool is \"planned\".\n- **Dates / done means:** UNKNOWN. No deadlines are set anywhere.\n\n## 4. HPI protocol manual\n- **KR 1.3** (SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md): \"HPI protocol v1 drafted — data integration, flow, storage, dashboarding, interpretation — circulated to Chris + Kenny… walked through with Kenny\". Due Aug 31; not scored.\n  - **Receiver: Chris Ruf + Kenny Boyd.** Also in JD-feedback-memo-2026-07-20.md:22.\n- **Status:** the 08-14 status report says \"No movement logged\". There are no HPI meetings July–September.\n- **This is one of Eric's JD lanes:** \"HPI protocol and its dashboarding\" (OKR doc). Exact JD wording: UNKNOWN.\n- **A separate existing draft:** ~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/HPI_RTP_Manual_Outline_V3.docx (plus V2, ORIGINAL). \"Return-to-Performance Manual… Effective Date: June 1, 2026 | Version 3.0 | Draft\", 13 sections.\n  - Eric owns sections 1, 2, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11; Jeremy owns 3–5; JB owns 10.\n  - Appendix A is \"NCAA Performance Technology Best Practices\".\n  - The June 1 target has lapsed (source: M/2026-04-15_RTP_04152026.md).\n  - KR 1.3 roughly maps to sections 6, 7, 9 and 11. The full manual depends on Jeremy and JB, which breaks the OKR rule \"critical path inside the unit's control\".\n- **\"Create the Manual\":** that phrase appears nowhere.\n- **Hard date / done means:** UNKNOWN beyond the lapsed Aug 31 and June 1 targets.\n\n## 5. NCAA best practices for data & technology\n- **Portfolio:** `NCAA_BestPractices_Doc` (job lane, rank 2, stage idea), \"Chris Ruf meeting deliverable\". It came from M/2026-07-30_Applied_Performance___Tech_Vetting_Staff_Onboarding__Website.md (32:15): \"favoring flexible best practice documents over rigid formal policies\".\n  - The folder ~/DEV/NCAA_BestPractices_Doc has an empty STATUS.\n  - It is \"Staged to Fall\" under Objective 1.\n- **Receiver:** Chris Ruf, as an inference from the portfolio purpose text.\n- **Webinar (2026-09-09, 45 min, NCAA SSI, speakers Tim Coffey and Mark Koberly/Coberly):**\n  - `/Users/kristinarash/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings/2026-09-09_NCAA_SSI_Webinar__Performance_Tech__Data_Governance.md` (Fireflies 01M23EEHZ3CRE03AYYADWA3N0D)\n  - `/Users/kristinarash/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/SSI_Notes_09092026.docx` (12 KB of text, dated Sep 10)\n  - No PDF or slides found after 09-05 in Downloads, Documents, Drive or OneDrive.\n- **Recommendations stated:**\n  - A written plan/policy for adopting technology (justification, validity/reliability, data ownership, access)\n  - Consult general counsel, IT and risk management\n  - Routinely re-evaluate whether each tool gives actionable value\n  - Educate staff, coaches and athletes before deploying anything\n  - Get athlete consent, with opt-out where feasible\n  - Collect athlete feedback\n  - Review vendor contracts for data resale\n  - Link medical and performance data\n- **\"Data continuity plan\" is not from the webinar.** It comes from the OKR doc: \"Staged to Fall: data-continuity plan per NCAA Best Practices document (what survives a staff transition)\".\n- **Earlier NCAA material:** Drive 01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/2026-03-05_SSI_PerformanceTechRecs/ (Action_Plan, Condensed, SSI_Summary_and_Recommendations, SSI_PerformanceTech_StaffOverview_v3.md) and ~/DEV/SoftwareTech_Mgmt_Framework/deliverables/NCAA_PerformanceTech_v3.docx.\n- **The 9/14 attestation item is unrelated.** It came from the student-services staff meeting (M/2026-09-14_Team_Sync…, 36:40): \"Finalize and circulate NCAA attestation report draft… end of September… submission by mid-October\". It is a student-athlete services compliance report (see M/2026-05-07 mental-health attestation and Drive 06_TEMPLATES/KB_Doc_Examples/NCAA Attestations Information - Baylor Athletics - SA Services - Fall 2025.docx). Nothing ties it to data/tech or to Eric.\n- **Hard date / done means:** UNKNOWN.\n\n## Staged to Fall / Fall OKR drafts\n- The \"Staged to Fall\" lists exist only in SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-OKRs-2026-27.md, dated 07-17, v3. Its Aug 31 section adds the Fall candidates \"continuity plan, white-paper publication, website distribution, Linda's role integration, data-management system build\". SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-Active-Projects.md lists NCAA_BestPractices_Doc as \"staged\".\n- **No Fall OKR set has been written.** Status report of 09-07: \"the Fall (Sep–Dec) set has not been authored\".\n- **Only files touched after 08-31:**\n  - SB/Inbox/status-reports/2026-09-07-status.md\n  - SB/Projects/Applied-Performance-Operating-Cadence.md (09-14)\n  - ~/DEV/project-triage/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-14-prioritization-system-design.md (Fall slate and build step \"Draft Fall KRs from… Staged to Fall\")"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf4MtdfmExtM2ih7moxdL","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ab08538-c2a7-4b4a-b4ff-b23fea8f9535","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:31:57.011Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
