{"parentUuid":"7e8da6d6-4496-4aca-a592-e0fc846d1d8c","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14657374 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6c38d8da-cf38-4b3a-b953-74f3fa52a7ab","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:31:58.134Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14657374 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6c38d8da-cf38-4b3a-b953-74f3fa52a7ab","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","attachment":{"type":"batching_reminder_sent","text":"First privately list what you need next; then request every item that doesn't depend on another's result in this one response.","model":"claude-opus-5[1m]"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5366c125-c5eb-4623-b902-f0fdb6be2aea","timestamp":"2026-09-15T01:31:58.141Z","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/project-triage","sessionId":"df3b3576-b317-408d-964a-187d57ed18ca","version":"2.1.271","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"5366c125-c5eb-4623-b902-f0fdb6be2aea","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a89be5bc70b9389ae","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf4MxGb7JygSVcb5hRTtd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've sent the full findings to the calling agent. Nothing else is needed: nothing left depends on another result, and there are no open requests.\n\n**What's missing in the charters:**\n- **Receivers:**\n  - Kenny Boyd for Tech Inventory and Chris Ruf for NCAA best practices are both inferred from the project list; I found no direct confirmation.\n  - Chris and Kenny for the HPI protocol is stated outright in the OKR doc.\n  - Joe Smith (assistant athletic trainer) for the Return to Performance course is stated in the course folder.\n  - Education Curriculum has no named receiver or requester.\n- **Dates:** the only hard dates are the Tech Inventory soft deadline of 29 September and two targets that have already passed for the HPI work (June 1 and August 31). The course and the NCAA document have no dates anywhere.\n- **Job-description wording:** unknown for all five. I couldn't find the job description itself on disk or on Drive.\n\n**Surprises the charters need to handle:**\n- **Tech Inventory:** only Volleyball is still outstanding as of 9/14. Micah Lamb in ITS hasn't replied in about 4 weeks.\n- **Education Curriculum:** this is not the project-list entry \"SportScience_Curriculum\", which is the intern curriculum. In the transcript, Toby Brooks is the other speaker. He's a practicum student helping out, not the person receiving the work. The 09-02 meeting gives two conflicting video dates: four videos \"by end of September\" and four \"mid October to early November.\"\n- **HPI manual:** there are two different things.\n  - The first is the OKR item \"HPI protocol v1\", Eric's own work.\n  - The second is a 13-section working-group draft at `~/DEV/RTP_WorkingGroup/Docs/HPI_RTP_Manual_Outline_V3.docx`, where Jeremy owns sections 3–5 and JB owns section 10.\n  - Chartering the whole manual breaks the OKR rule that a result can't depend on someone outside the unit. The phrase \"Create the Manual\" appears nowhere.\n- **NCAA best practices:**\n  - The webinar was on 2026-09-09. There are two sources: the vault note `~/SecondBrain/Inbox/meetings/2026-09-09_NCAA_SSI_Webinar__Performance_Tech__Data_Governance.md` and Eric's own notes at `~/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-BaylorUniversity/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/SSI_Notes_09092026.docx`. I found no PDF or slides.\n  - Its main recommendations:\n    - a written plan for adopting new technology\n    - review by legal, IT and risk management\n    - regular checks that each tool is still worth keeping\n    - training for staff and coaches\n    - athlete consent with the option to opt out\n    - checking vendor contracts for data resale\n  - The \"data continuity plan\" comes from the OKR doc's \"Staged to Fall\" list, not from the webinar.\n  - The 9/14 \"NCAA attestation report\" is a student-services compliance item and has nothing to do with this project.\n- **Fall OKRs:** none have been written. The only \"Staged to Fall\" lists are in the July OKR doc. The only planning files changed after 08-31 are the 09-07 status report, the Operating Cadence page, and today's prioritization design spec."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4213,"cache_read_input_tokens":181544,"output_tokens":1139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4213},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":32,"output_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":181544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4213,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4213,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type